{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'land.draw|Terrain|rig.pose|audio.*ctx|audio.*music|class Synth|gain|settings.*onChange' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -65 && sed -n '169,190p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && sed -n '7780,7830p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '9269,9320p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"106:- 1744 Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js); E.Terrain: terrain\n252:- `game.screen.resize()`: fit the buffer to the canvas again (on window resize; after changing sizing options, setOptions does it)\n321:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. E [... omitted end of long line]\n403:- `game.particles.ground = null` †: null (the floor is z 0), or (x, y, z) -> the floor's height under a particle (a side-scroller's platforms, a 3D level: engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js sets it), asked again  [... omitted end of long line]\n415:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background characte [... omitted end of long line]\n501:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom) [... omitted end of long line]\n510:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | [... omitted end of long line]\n523:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n578:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value [... omitted end of long line]\n676:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Charact [... omitted end of long line]\n711:- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guar [... omitted end of long line]\n932:- `hero.wallSlide = 70`: the slowest fall against a wall\n1041:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1067:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n1068:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n1069:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n1070:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute a [... omitted end of long line]\n1071:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: thi [... omitted end of long line]\n1073:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n1074:- `game.audio.instrument(name, fn)` †: an instrument of the game's own: fn(ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) makes a note's sound (Web Audio, into bus, from time); its name is a wave a music track (wave [... omitted end of long line]\n1076:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token pe [... omitted end of long line]\n1078:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n1079:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop),  [... omitted end of long line]\n1082:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pi [... omitted end of long line]\n1083:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4) [... omitted end of long line]\n1084:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n1085:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n1087:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1088:- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n1089:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n1091:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n1093:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1095:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n1186:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HT [... omitted end of long line]\n1204:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (stri [... omitted end of long line]\n1247:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title'  [... omitted end of long line]\n1254:- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1388:- `E.Fighter.exchange(a, b)` †: settle one step between two fighters (E.Match calls it after both update): hits (both may land: a trade), shots against each other and against the fighters, push boxes  [... omitted end of long line]\n1445:- `E.gen.bsp(w, h, o = {})`: binary space partition: halves split again down to o.min (7) cells, a room in each leaf, sisters joined\n1521:- `mode7.fullRes(game, on)`: draw at the screen's own pixels (on, called each step: sharper, slower) or the game's again (off); returns the pixel size the game had (1 when it had no other)\n1523:- `mode7.refresh()`: forget the floor's baked texture (after changing the map or the function: it bakes again)\n1571:- `rhythm.hit(lane)` †: a press in a lane: judged against the nearest note there within the good window (a hold starts held)\n1665:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\n1739:- `E.choose(agent, options)` †: the option that best meets an agent's needs ({ gives: { hunger: -.6 }, x, y, cost }): each need it lowers, weighted by that need squared (the urgent first), less the wa [... omitted end of long line]\n1746:- `new E.Terrain(o = {}) → terrain`: new E.Terrain({ w, h, x, y, materials, chunk }): see the manual\n1764:- `terrain.drawn = 0`: how many chunks the last draw painted again\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n   *  to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its level is\n   *  voiceVolume) or 'master'. Returns a GainNode, or null where there is no sound (headless, no Web Audio) */\n  bus(name = 'sfx') {\n    if (!['sfx', 'music', 'voice', 'master'].includes(name)) warn('bus:' + name, 'audio.bus(\"' + name + '\"): no such bus (sfx, music, voice, master): the sfx bus');\n    if (this._game.headless || !this._init()) return null;\n    return name === 'master' ? this._master : name === 'music' ? this._musBus : name === 'voice' ? this._voiceBus : this._sfxBus;\n  }\n  /** set the master volume, 0..1 */\n  setVolume(v) { this.volume = clamp(v, 0, 1); this.applyVolume(); }\n  /** toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state */\n  mute(on = !this.muted) { this.muted = on; this.applyVolume(); return on; }\n  /** the page is hidden (sleep true) or back: the sound sleeps with it unless the player keeps it on (settings.background) */\n  _background(sleep) { const c = this.ctx; if (!c) return; try { if (sleep && c.state === 'running') { this._slept = true; c.suspend().catch(() => {}); } else if (!sleep && this._slept) { this._slept = false; c.resume().catch(() => {}); } } catch (e) { /* closed */ } }\n  /** quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused */\n  duck(on = true) { on = !!on; if (this.ducked === on) return; this.ducked = on; this.applyVolume(); }\n  _duck(on) { if (this._ducked === on) return; this._ducked = on; this.applyVolume(); }   // (the engine's own: game.paused)\n  _pulse(duty) {\n    if (this._waves[duty]) return this._waves[duty];\n    const N = 40, re = new Float32Array(N), im = new Float32Array(N);\n    for (let n = 1; n < N; n++) { const a = 2 / (n * Math.PI) * Math.sin(n * Math.PI * duty); re[n] = a * Math.cos(n * Math.PI * duty); im[n] = a * Math.sin(n * Math.PI * duty); }\n    return (this._waves[duty] = this.ctx.createPeriodicWave(re, im));\n  }\n  // one voice at t0 into bus: its sources (a looped one sounds on, at its volume, until they are stopped)\n  _voice(p, bus, t0, mul = 1, loop = false) {\n    const c = this.ctx, wave = p.wave || 'square', dur = Math.max(.012, p.dur || .15), vol = p.vol === undefined ? .3 : p.vol, att = p.attack === undefined ? .004 : p.attack;\n    const t = t0 + (p.delay || 0), end = t + dur, f0 = Math.max(20, noteFreq(p.freq || 440) * mul), to = p.to ? Math.max(20, noteFreq(p.to) * mul) : 0;\n    const ins = this._ins && this._ins[wave]; if (ins) { ins(c, bus, t, f0, dur, vol); return []; }   // (an instrument of the game's own)\n    const g = c.createGain(); g.gain.setValueAtTime(0, t); g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol, t + att);\n    if (loop) g.gain.setValueAtTime(vol, t + att);   // (held at its volume until stopped)\n    else if (p.hold) { g.gain.setValueAtTime(vol, Math.max(t + att, end - .03)); g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(0, end); }\n    else g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0005, end);\n    let lfo = null;\n    let src;\n    if (wave === 'noise') {\n      src = c.createBufferSource(); src.buffer = this._noise; src.loop = true;\n      const f = c.createBiquadFilter(); f.type = p.filter || 'bandpass'; f.Q.value = p.q || 1.1; f.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0, t); if (to) f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(to, end);\n      src.connect(f); f.connect(g); src.start(t, this._rnd() * .5);\n    } else {\n      src = c.createOscillator();\n      if (wave === 'pulse' || wave === 'pulse12') src.setPeriodicWave(this._pulse(wave === 'pulse' ? .25 : .125));\n      else src.type = wave === 'saw' ? 'sawtooth' : ['square', 'triangle', 'sine', 'sawtooth'].includes(wave) ? wave : 'square';\n      src.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0, t);\n      if (to) src.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(to, end);\n      if (p.arp) { const st = p.step || .06; for (let k = 0, tt = t; tt < end; tt += st, k++) src.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0 * Math.pow(2, p.arp[p.loop ? k % p.arp.length : Math.min(k, p.arp.length - 1)] / 12), tt); }\n      if (p.vib) { lfo = c.createOscillator(); const lg = c.createGain(); lfo.frequency.value = p.vib[0]; lg.gain.value = f0 * p.vib[1]; lfo.connect(lg); lg.connect(src.frequency); lfo.start(t); if (!loop) lfo.stop(end + .05); }\n      src.connect(g); src.start(t);\n    }\n    g.connect(bus); if (!loop) src.stop(end + .05);\n    return lfo ? [src, lfo] : [src];\n  }\n  /**\nclass Menu {\n  constructor(game, items, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; items: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled }); i: the one under the cursor; active:\n     *  false stops it reading input */\n    this.game = game; this.items = items || []; this.i = 0; this.active = true;\n    /** x, y: where it sits, 'center' or pixels; title: a heading, or null; box: draw a window round it; color: the\n     *  entries' color; pick: the color of the one under the cursor; dim: disabled entries' color; bg, border: the\n     *  window's colors; onPick: called (i, item) on confirm; onCancel: called on cancel; onMove: called (i, item)\n     *  when the cursor moves; sound: false silences it; input: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so\n     *  any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's); scale: its text and rows that many times (2, 3:\n     *  across a room on a TV); rows: at most that many entries shown, the list scrolling under its cursor (0: all) */\n    Object.assign(this, { x: 'center', y: 'center', title: null, box: true, color: '#ffffff', pick: '#ffd36a', dim: '#6a6488', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', onPick: null, onCancel: null, onMove: null, sound: true, input: null, scale: 1, rows: 0 }, o);\n    this._skip(1);\n  }\n  _label(it) { return typeof it === 'string' ? it : it.label; }\n  _off(it) { return typeof it === 'object' && it.disabled; }\n  _skip(dir) { for (let k = 0; k < this.items.length && this._off(this.items[this.i]); k++) this.i = (this.i + dir + this.items.length) % this.items.length; }\n  /** the entry under the cursor */\n  get selected() { return this.items[this.i]; }\n  // where it sits, from its items and the screen's size (update and draw both: a click picks an entry with no draw yet)\n  _layout() {\n    const S = this.game.screen, k = Math.max(1, Math.round(this.scale || 1)), fo = { scale: k }, labels = this.items.map(it => this._label(it)), n = labels.length;\n    const w = Math.max(E.font.width(this.title || '', fo), ...labels.map(l => E.font.width(l, fo))) + 22 * k, rowH = E.font.lineHeight(fo) + 2 * k, vis = this.rows > 0 ? Math.min(n, this.rows) : n;\n    let first = clamp(this._first || 0, 0, Math.max(0, n - vis)); if (this.i < first) first = this.i; else if (this.i >= first + vis) first = this.i - vis + 1; this._first = first;   // (the cursor's row in view)\n    const h = vis * rowH + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0) + 8 * k, x = this.x === 'center' ? Math.round((S.W - w) / 2) : this.x, y = this.y === 'center' ? Math.round((S.H - h) / 2) : this.y;\n    const top = y + 5 * k + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0); this._box = { x: x + 3 * k, y: top - 2 * k, w: w - 6 * k, rowH, first, vis };   // (where the entries are, for a click or tap)\n    return { labels, w, h, x, y, top, rowH, k, fo, first, vis };\n  }\n  /** entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and\n   *  feed('up') there); null while it is scrolled out of view */\n  rowAt(i) { this._layout(); const b = this._box; return i < b.first || i >= b.first + b.vis ? null : [b.x, b.y + (i - b.first) * b.rowH, b.w, b.rowH]; }\n  /** move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an\n   *  entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled */\n  update() {\n    if (!this.active || !this.items.length) return false;\n    this._layout();\n    const P = this.input ? [this.input] : this.game._players || [this.game.input], inp = P[0], any = f => P.some(f), n = this.items.length, old = this.i, b = this._box;\n    const row = p => { if (!b || !p || p[0] < b.x || p[0] >= b.x + b.w) return -1; const r = Math.floor((p[1] - b.y) / b.rowH), k = b.first + r; return r >= 0 && r < b.vis && k < n && !this._off(this.items[k]) ? k : -1; };\n    if (any(I => I.repeat('up'))) { this.i = (this.i + n - 1) % n; this._skip(-1); }\n    if (any(I => I.repeat('down'))) { this.i = (this.i + 1) % n; this._skip(1); }\n    if (inp.mouse.t !== this._mt) { this._mt = inp.mouse.t; const k = row(inp.pointer()); if (k >= 0) this.i = k; }   // the mouse moved over an entry\n    const tap = row(inp.clicked());   // a click or tap on an entry picks it\n    if (tap >= 0) this.i = tap;\n    if (this.i !== old) { if (this.sound) this.game.audio.sfx('select'); if (this.onMove) this.onMove(this.i, this.items[this.i]); }\n    if ((any(I => I.pressed('confirm')) || tap >= 0) && !this._off(this.items[this.i])) { if (this.sound) this.game.audio.sfx('confirm'); P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); if (this.onPick) this.onPick(this.i, this.items[this.i]); return true; }\n    if (any(I => I.pressed('cancel')) && this.onCancel) { if (this.sound) this.game.audio.sfx('cancel'); P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); this.onCancel(); return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n  /** draw it to the overlay */\n  draw(r) {\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      const { labels, w, h, x, y, top: yy, rowH, k: K, first, vis } = this._layout(), T = { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a', scale: K };\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Humanoid.pose|poses\\\\[|handR.*\\\\[|_step\\\\(\\\\).*' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -24 && sed -n '1744,1770p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '9805,9865p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Humanoid.pose|poses\\\\[|handR.*\\\\[|_step\\\\(\\\\).*' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -24 && sed -n '1744,1770p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '9805,9865p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"2939:    if (this.shell) this.shell._step();   // its screens move the focus with this step's input, and hold it back from the game\n4125:  hand(which = 'R') { const w = this._w(this.J['hand' + which] || this.J.handR); return [this.x + w[0], this.y + w[1], this.z + w[2]]; }\n4127:  tip() { const J = this.J, W = HUMANOID_WEAPONS[this.o.weapon], l = W ? W.length : this.o.bladeLen, L = typeof l === 'function' ? l(this) : l, w = this._w(V3.add(J.handR, V3.mul(J.bladeDir, L))); ret [... omitted end of long line]\n4142:   *   E.Humanoid.pose's, tilt (radians: the whole body forward about the feet, a dive) and roll (sideways),\n4244:    const OW = this._ownW || (this._ownW = {});   // a game's own held poses (E.Humanoid.pose), eased in and out as state.pose names them, over the solve\n4452:      if (p === J.handR) return S(p[0] + df, p[1] + dr, p[2] + dz);\n4648:      const sh = s > 0 ? Q.shR : Q.shL, el = s > 0 ? Q.elbowR : Q.elbowL, hd = s > 0 ? Q.handR : Q.handL, far = el[2] < dC;\n4715:      const sh = s > 0 ? Q.shR : Q.shL, el = s > 0 ? Q.elbowR : Q.elbowL, hd = s > 0 ? Q.handR : Q.handL, far = el[2] < dC;\n4734:    return { style, g, rig: this, o: this.o, C: this.C, J, Q, Sp, u, ops, cap, hd, bd, hand: Q.handR, at: (t, dx = 0, dy = 0, dz = 0) => Sp(hd, bd[0] * t + dx, bd[1] * t + dy, bd[2] * t + dz), push: ( [... omitted end of long line]\n4785:    for (const k of ['hipL', 'hipR', 'kneeL', 'kneeR', 'footL', 'footR', 'shL', 'shR', 'elbowL', 'elbowR', 'handL', 'handR', 'head']) { const p = P(J[k]); px.dot(g, p[0], p[1], '#ffffff'); }\n4795:/** held poses of a game's own (state.pose: an id), by id: E.Humanoid.pose(id, (J, w, rig) => ...) adds one */\n4800:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, Lb = o.bladeLen, Hn = Q.handR, sl = Math.hypot(bd[0], bd[1]) || 1, gx = -bd[1] / sl * 1.8, gy = bd[0] / sl * 1.8;\n4812:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, L = o.bladeLen, Hn = Q.handR, sl = Math.hypot(bd[0], bd[1]) || 1, sx = -bd[1] / sl * 1.6, sy = bd[0] / sl * 1.6;\n4826:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, Hn = Q.handR, mz = Sp(hd, bd[0] * 5.5, bd[1] * 5.5, bd[2] * 5.5), gp = Sp(hd, -bd[0] * .6, -bd[1] * .6, -bd[2] * .6 - 1.4), m = tones(C.metal);\n4829:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, Hn = Q.handR, mz = Sp(hd, bd[0] * 5, bd[1] * 5, bd[2] * 5), gp = Sp(hd, -bd[0] * .6, -bd[1] * .6, -bd[2] * .6 - 1.2);\n4836:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, Hn = Q.handR, top = Sp(hd, bd[0] * 10, bd[1] * 10, bd[2] * 10), bot = Sp(hd, -bd[0] * 7, -bd[1] * 7, -bd[2] * 7), wt = tones(C.staff || '#8a5a32'), ot = tones( [... omitted end of long line]\n4839:    const hd = J.handR, bd = J.bladeDir, Hn = Q.handR, top = Sp(hd, bd[0] * 10, bd[1] * 10, bd[2] * 10), bot = Sp(hd, -bd[0] * 7, -bd[1] * 7, -bd[2] * 7);\n4874:Humanoid.poses = HUMANOID_POSES;\n4884:Humanoid.pose = (id, fn) => { HUMANOID_POSES[id] = fn; return fn; };\n9805:  _step() {\n## Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js)\n\n- `new E.Terrain(o = {}) → terrain`: new E.Terrain({ w, h, x, y, materials, chunk }): see the manual\n- `terrain.add(x, y, r, id)`: fill a circle with a material\n- `terrain.addPoly(points, id)`: a material inside a polygon of world points\n- `terrain.carve(x, y, r, o = {})`: a crater: air within r of (x, y) but for hard materials; o.particles: bits of what it took fly out; returns { id: cells taken }\n- `terrain.carvePoly(points)`: air inside a polygon of world points (hard materials stay)\n- `terrain.collider()`: a field for the physics module: world.add(land.collider())\n- `terrain.draw(r)`: draw it as decals under the bodies, in the side view (its y is the engine's z); only changed chunks are redrawn\n- `terrain.fill(fn)`: set every cell from fn(x, y) (the world point at the cell's middle) -> a material id or 0\n- `terrain.get(x, y)`: the material at a world point (0: air, and outside)\n- `terrain.ground(x, y)`: the top of the first solid ground at or below (x, y) (a world y), or null when there is none\n- `terrain.hit(x, y, r)`: a circle in the ground: [nx, ny, depth] (out along the normal by depth clears it), or null\n- `terrain.normal(x, y, r = 4)`: the ground's normal near (x, y): [nx, ny], pointing away from the solid within r\n- `terrain.ray(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: the first solid cell on the line from (x0, y0) to (x1, y1): [x, y] (the last air before it), or null\n- `terrain.set(x, y, id)`: set the cell at a world point\n- `terrain.solid(x, y)`: is the point in the ground?\n- `terrain.walk(b, dt, o = {})`: a walker's step: up and down slopes of up to climb, stopped by walls, falling and landing (see the manual)\n- `terrain.cells`: the mask, row by row from the top (0: air)\n- `terrain.chunk`: the drawn squares' size\n- `terrain.drawn = 0`: how many chunks the last draw painted again\n- `terrain.h`, `terrain.w`: its size in cells (world units)\n- `terrain.materials`: their looks (a material's id is its index + 1)\n- `terrain.x`, `terrain.y`: its bottom left corner\n  _step() {\n    const g = this._game, I = g.input, now = g.real, sc = g.scene, play = !!sc && (!!sc.pausable || g.sceneName === 'main');\n    const pause = this._pauseSpec() && (!this._sys || (g.pauseOverlay !== false && play));   // (the engine's own menu stays out of a game that draws its own pause)\n    if (pause && g.paused && !this._stack.length) this.show('pause');\n    if (!g.paused && this._stack.length && (this._ownPause || (pause && this._stack.some(t => t.name === 'pause')))) { this._stack.length = 0; this._ownPause = false; this._capEnd(); this._render(); }   // resumed from code\n    if (this.root) {\n      if (this._toastEnd && now > this._toastEnd) { this._els.toast.classList.remove('on'); this._toastEnd = 0; }\n      if (this._tutEnd && now > this._tutEnd) this.tutorial(null);\n      this.root.classList.toggle('esh-still', !!g.reduceMotion);\n    }\n    if (!this._stack.length) return;\n    const keep = this._held; this._held = new Set();\n    const has = a => !!I.map[a], confirm = has('confirm') && I.pressed('confirm'), cancel = has('cancel') && I.pressed('cancel'), closeAll = has('pause') && I.pressed('pause'), mv = I.move();\n    const hit = ['up', 'down', 'left', 'right'].find(a => has(a) && I.pressed(a)), dir = Math.abs(mv[1]) > .5 ? (mv[1] < 0 ? 'up' : 'down') : Math.abs(mv[0]) > .5 ? (mv[0] < 0 ? 'left' : 'right') : null;\n    for (const a in I.map) if (!keep.has(a)) I.suppress(a);   // the game doesn't see what the menu used\n    if (this._cap) { this._capPad(); return; }   // binding: the next button is the answer, not a move in the menu\n    if (!this.root) { if (cancel) this.back(); else if (closeAll) this.hide(); return; }\n    if (hit) { this._dir = hit; this._dirT = now + .35; this._nav(hit); }   // a press (however short), then the held direction repeats\n    else if (dir !== this._dir) { this._dir = dir; this._dirT = now + .35; if (dir) this._nav(dir); }\n    else if (dir && now > this._dirT) { this._dirT = now + .09; this._nav(dir); }\n    const f = document.activeElement, mine = f && this._els.scr.contains(f);\n    if (confirm && mine && f.tagName === 'BUTTON') f.click();\n    else if (cancel) this.back();\n    else if (closeAll) this.hide();   // Start (or P) closes the whole menu; Escape and B go back one screen\n  }\n  /** binding a controller button: the first one pressed since binding began (Start cancels) */\n  _capPad() {\n    const c = this._cap, I = this._ctlI(); if (!c || c.device !== 'pad') return;\n    const i = I.padPrev.findIndex((on, k) => on && !c.prev[k]); c.prev = I.padPrev.slice();\n    const ra = RSTICK.find(k => I.held.has(k) && !c.prevR.includes(k)); c.prevR = RSTICK.filter(k => I.held.has(k));   // (the right stick pushed: its direction)\n    if (i === 9) this._capEnd('Not changed.'); else if (i >= 0) this._capBind('Pad' + i); else if (ra) this._capBind(ra);\n  }\n  /** move the focus (or turn a focused slider or choice), keeping it in view */\n  _nav(dir) {\n    const all = this._focusables(); if (!all.length) return;\n    const f = document.activeElement, i = all.indexOf(f), side = dir === 'left' || dir === 'right', d = dir === 'up' || dir === 'left' ? -1 : 1;\n    if (f && side && f.type === 'range') { if (d < 0) f.stepDown(); else f.stepUp(); f.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); return; }\n    if (f && side && f._cycle) { f._cycle(d); return; }\n    const n = all[((i < 0 ? 0 : i + d) + all.length) % all.length]; n.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (n.scrollIntoView) n.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });\n  }\n}\nE.Shell = Shell;\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 22. GPU LIGHTING (WebGPU)  optional. game.enableGPU({ map }) turns it on.\n *    The Canvas renderer still draws every color. Alongside it, it writes an\n *    \"info\" image (height, surface type, glow per pixel). The GPU then lights each\n *    pixel: colored point lights, soft shadows marched through a heightmap of the\n *    level, light wrapping around characters (normals from their silhouettes),\n *    glow spilling onto nearby surfaces, dithered light bands, and heat shimmer.\n *    If WebGPU is missing or fails, the game keeps the Canvas lighting.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst WGSL_COMMON = /* wgsl */`\nstruct Params {\n  a: vec4f, b: vec4f, c: vec4f, camv: vec4f,\n  right: vec4f, up: vec4f, amb: vec4f, fx: vec4f,\n  mapd: vec4f, scr: vec4f, scr2: vec4f, bufd: vec4f,\n  nheat: vec4f, p0: vec4f, p1: vec4f, p2: vec4f,\n  lights: array<vec4f, 64>,\n  heat: array<vec4f, 8>,\n};\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/content.js'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"'....W..W.W'\\\",\\\"'....W..W'\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > src/audio.js <<'EOF'\n// Every sound is synthesized. Native music/effects/voice buses own the user's gain exactly once.\nexport function formant(ctx,bus,time,freq=190,duration=.13,vol=.055,index=0) {\n const osc=ctx.createOscillator(),filter=ctx.createBiquadFilter(),gain=ctx.createGain();\n osc.type='sawtooth';osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq,time);osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(freq*(index%2?1.35:.8),time+duration);\n filter.type='bandpass';filter.frequency.value=[780,1200,1700,950][index%4];filter.Q.value=4;\n gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0,time);gain.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol,time+.012);gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,time+duration);\n osc.connect(filter).connect(gain).connect(bus);osc.start(time);osc.stop(time+duration+.02);osc.onended=()=>{osc.disconnect();filter.disconnect();gain.disconnect();};return osc;\n}\nexport function lute(ctx,bus,time,freq,dur,vol) {\n const osc=ctx.createOscillator(),g=ctx.createGain(),f=ctx.createBiquadFilter();osc.type='triangle';osc.frequency.value=freq;f.type='lowpass';f.frequency.setValueAtTime(3500,time);f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(500,time+Math.max(.04,dur));\n g.gain.setValueAtTime(0,time);g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol,time+.004);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,time+Math.max(.04,dur));osc.connect(f).connect(g).connect(bus);osc.start(time);osc.stop(time+dur+.04);osc.onended=()=>{osc.disconnect();f.disconnect();g.disconnect();};\n}\nexport const MARCH = {bpm:104,steps:4,tracks:[\n {wave:'siegeLute',vol:.13,notes:'D4 . A4 . D5 - C5 . B4 . A4 . G4 . E4 . | F4 . A4 . D5 . F5 - E5 . D5 . C5 . A4 . | G4 . B4 . E5 . D5 . C5 . A4 . F4 . E4 . | D4 . F4 . A4 . D5 - A4 . F4 . D4 - . .'},\n {wave:'triangle',vol:.12,notes:'D3 . . . A2 . . . D3 . . . A2 . . . | F3 . . . C3 . . . F3 . . . A2 . . . | G2 . . . D3 . . . A2 . . . A2 . . . | D3 . . . A2 . . . D3 . . . D3 . . .'},\n {wave:'drums',vol:.045,notes:'k . . h . . s . k . h . s . . h'}]};\nexport class SiegeAudio {\n constructor(game){this.game=game;this.lastVoice=-100;this.voices=[];this.ended=false;const a=game.audio;a.instrument('siegeLute',lute);\n const patches={\n siegeWind:{wave:'noise',freq:260,to:450,dur:.06,vol:.06},siegeLaunch:[{wave:'noise',freq:650,to:130,dur:.17,vol:.12},{wave:'triangle',freq:95,to:45,dur:.13,vol:.13}],\n siegeStone:[{wave:'noise',freq:950,to:110,dur:.24,vol:.12},{wave:'sine',freq:130,to:45,dur:.2,vol:.15}],\n siegeWood:{wave:'noise',freq:1700,to:300,dur:.17,vol:.14},siegeCrew:{wave:'triangle',freq:440,to:230,dur:.16,vol:.10},\n siegeArmor:[{wave:'square',freq:180,to:75,dur:.12,vol:.07},{wave:'sine',freq:840,to:420,dur:.24,vol:.06}],\n siegeWater:{wave:'sine',freq:320,to:70,dur:.24,vol:.14},siegeRepair:{wave:'triangle',freq:370,to:210,dur:.045,vol:.09},\n siegeReturn:{wave:'triangle',freq:440,arp:[0,4,7,12],step:.06,dur:.26,vol:.10},siegeCancel:{wave:'sine',freq:240,to:140,dur:.09,vol:.06}};\n for(const k in patches)a.define(k,patches[k]);}\n music(court=0){if(this.ended)return;const song={...MARCH,bpm:[104,96,112,86,123][court],tracks:MARCH.tracks};this.game.audio.music(song,{sync:true});}\n voice(variant=0){if(this.ended||this.game.real-this.lastVoice<3)return;this.lastVoice=this.game.real;const a=this.game.audio,bus=a.bus('voice'),ctx=a.ctx;if(\"'!ctx||!bus||ctx.state!=='\"'running')return;\n for(let i=0;i<4;i++)this.voices.push(formant(ctx,bus,ctx.currentTime+i*.105,variant?145+i*13:210-i*15,.1,.09,i+variant));this.voices=this.voices.filter(o=>o.context.currentTime<o.context.currentTime+1).slice(-20);}\n event(e){if(this.ended)return;const a=this.game.audio;if(e.type==='launch')a.sfx('siegeLaunch',{pitch:e.stone===1?.72:1});\n else if(e.type==='wind')a.sfx('siegeWind');else if(e.type==='cancel')a.sfx('siegeCancel');\n else if(e.type==='water')a.sfx('siegeWater');else if(e.type==='recovery')a.sfx('siegeReturn');\n else if(e.type==='hit'){a.sfx(e.kind==='crew'?'siegeCrew':e.kind==='launcher'?'siegeArmor':'siegeStone');if(e.kind\"'!=='\"'castle')this.voice(e.seat);}\n else if(e.type==='collapse'){a.sfx('siegeWood',{pitch:.7});this.voice(1);}\n else if(e.type==='split')a.sfx('whoosh',{vol:.25,pitch:1.4});else if(e.type==='outcome'){this.fanfare(e.winner);this.voice(1);}}\n fanfare(winner){this.game.audio.sting({bpm:136,steps:4,tracks:[{wave:'triangle',vol:.18,notes:winner<0?'D4 - F4 - E4 - D4 -':'D4 . D4 . A4 - F#4 - A4 - D5 - - - - -'},{wave:'siegeLute',vol:.10,notes:'D3 - A3 - D4 - - - D3 - A3 - D4 - - -'}]});}\n reset(){for(const v of this.voices)try{v.stop();}catch{}this.voices=[];this.lastVoice=-100;this.game.audio.stopMusic(0);}\n stop(){this.reset();this.ended=true;this.game.audio.mute(true);try{this.game.audio.ctx?.suspend()?.catch(()=>{});}catch{}}\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/view.js <<'EOF'\nimport { ARENA, STONES, DT, clamp } from './config.js';\nimport { COURTS } from './content.js';\nimport { powerOf, predict, remaining, readyAt } from './sim.js';\nexport const TEAM = [{color:'#75dfd4',dark:'#245e64',name:'THE TEAL TROUPE'},{color:'#ff9c75',dark:'#843e4b',name:'THE CORAL COURT'}];\nexport class Battlefield {\n constructor(game,E){this.game=game;this.E=E;this.world=null;this.debris=[];this.ripples=[];this.flashes=[];this.poses=[];this.guidance=[800,160];this.debug=false;this.arc=false;this.selection=null;this.preview=null;\n E.VIEWS.siege=new E.View('siege','Tournament',0,0,1,1);\n for(const c of COURTS)E.MATERIALS[\"'`siegeStone${c.id}`]={color:c.stone,pattern:'\"'stones',size:6,over:[['cracks'],['moss','#68805c',{amount:.15}]]};\n E.SHAPES.siegeBlock={about:'An individually destructible tournament ashlar',mats:{s:'stone'},params:{w:19,h:18},make:p=>[['box','s',[0,0,0],[p.w,11,p.h]]]};\n E.SHAPES.siegeTimber={about:'Braced timber tower section',mats:{s:'oak',b:'walnut'},params:{w:19,h:18},make:p=>[['box','s',[0,0,0],[p.w,11,p.h]],['box','b',[0,6,0],[2,1,p.h]],['box','b',[0,6,p.h-3],[p.w,1,2]]]};\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeHaul',(J,w,rig)=>{const t=rig.t*12;for(const [id,phase]of[['handR',0],['handL',Math.PI]]){J[id][0]+=(8+Math.cos(t+phase)*3-J[id][0])*w;J[id][2]+=(17+Math.sin(t+phase)*3-J[id][2])*w;}J.head[0]+=3*w;});\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeTools',(J,w,rig)=>{J.handR[0]+=(9-J.handR[0])*w;J.handR[2]+=(12+Math.sin(rig.t*16)*5-J.handR[2])*w;J.handL[2]+=(17-J.handL[2])*w;});\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeFlag',(J,w)=>{J.handR[0]+=(8-J.handR[0])*w;J.handR[2]+=(26-J.handR[2])*w;});\n this.crews=[0,1].map(seat=>[0,1].map(i=>new E.Humanoid({size:.86,build:i?'bulky':'heroic',outfit:'tunic',hat:i?'band':'helmet',weapon:null,sleeves:'long',hair:i?'short':'spiky',seed:seat*20+i+4,colors:{cloth:TEAM[seat].color,pants:'#333e56',hair:i?'#b9844f':'#e8c17c',trim:'#eed7a1',skin:i?'#c69a78':'#e7bfa0',metal:'#9babc0',boot:'#352c35'}})));\n this.spectators=Array.from({length:15},(_,i)=>new E.Humanoid({size:.58,hat:i%3?'cap':'crown',outfit:i%2?'robe':'tunic',weapon:null,seed:40+i,colors:{cloth:['#8d4857','#69775a','#9a8553','#567e8b'][i%4],trim:'#c5ac72',skin:i%3?'#d8ae8b':'#a67c65'}}));\n }\n reset(w){this.world=w;this.debris=[];this.ripples=[];this.flashes=[];this.preview=null;this.predKey='';const c=w.courtDef;\n this.bg=new this.E.Backdrop({sky:c.id===3?['#111a3b','#465175','#ba7d79']:c.id===0?['#668ba2','#aac0b9','#e4d2aa']:['#3f506e','#9d8b8d','#ebc49c'],sun:c.id===3?undefined:{x:.52,y:.28,r:25,color:'#f4d9a7'},moon:c.id===3?{x:.53,y:.24,r:20,color:'#ece0b8'}:undefined,stars:c.id===3?60:0,layers:[{kind:'mountains',color:c.id===3?'#28334d':'#8c9699',y:.50,height:.20,parallax:.1},{kind:'castle',color:c.id===3?'#354157':'#a3a795',y:.66,height:.13,parallax:.2},{kind:'clouds',color:c.id===3?'#58526e':'#dfd4bd',y:.18,height:.13,parallax:.3,drift:2},{kind:'hills',color:c.id===3?'#324853':'#869780',y:.74,height:.14,parallax:.4}]});\n this.land=new this.E.Terrain({w:960,h:70,y:-34,materials:[{color:c.id===1?'#9c8865':'#777061',top:c.grass,edge:'#343a41',depth:5},{color:'#4f535a',top:'#71767a',edge:'#30343d',depth:3}],chunk:64});\n this.land.fill((x,z)=>x<307||x>653?z<ARENA.ground?(z<13?2:1):0:0);\n this.game.lights.enabled=true;this.game.lights.ambient=c.id===3?.7:.92;\n this.game.particles.ground=(x,y,z)=>x<307||x>653?ARENA.ground:ARENA.water;\n }\n update(dt,{seat=0,assist=false,reduced=false,title=false}={}){const w=this.world;if(\"'!w)return;this.reduced=reduced;const g=this.game;\n // Fit the whole lane. Portrait leaves room for a readable target inset above it.\n const ppu=Math.min(g.W/1000,g.H/440);g.view.zoom=ppu;g.view._siegeZoom=ppu; // View axes are refreshed via setZoom below when changed.\n if(Math.abs((g.zoom||1)-ppu)>.003){g.setZoom(ppu);}\n g.cam.smooth=0;g.cam.bounds=null;g.focus(480,0,130);\n for(let s=0;s<2;s++){const p=w.players[s],end=Math.max(p.crewUntil,p.launcherUntil),missing=w.tick<end,retreat=missing?clamp((end-w.tick)*DT*2,0,1):0;\n this.crews[s].forEach((rig,i)=>{const repair=w.tick<p.launcherUntil,charge=p.charge>=0,win=w.outcome?.winner===s;\n const x=ARENA.crew[s]+(s?-1:1)*(i?-17:0)+(s?1:-1)*retreat*28;\n const pose=w.outcome?(win?'\"'cheer':'siegeFlag'):missing?(repair?'siegeTools':'down'):charge?'siegeHaul':'hips';\n rig.update(dt,{x,y:i?4:0,z:ARENA.ground,facing:s?Math.PI:0,pose,expr:missing?'wince':win?'smile':charge?'angry':null,run:retreat>0?.8:0});});}\n this.spectators.forEach((rig,i)=>rig.update(dt,{x:340+i*20,y:15,z:30,facing:i%2?0:Math.PI,pose:w.outcome?'cheer':i%4===0?'wave':'hips'}));\n for(const d of this.debris){d.life-=dt;d.vz-=300*dt;d.x+=d.vx*dt;d.z+=d.vz*dt;d.rot+=dt*d.spin;if(d.z<ARENA.water&&d.life>.35)d.life=.35;}\n this.debris=this.debris.filter(d=>d.life>0);this.ripples=this.ripples.filter(d=>(d.life-=dt)>0);this.flashes=this.flashes.filter(d=>(d.life-=dt)>0);\n const p=w.players[seat],power=powerOf(w,p),key=[w.revision,p.stone,Math.round(power*150),assist].join(':');\n if(p.charge>=0&&key\"'!==this.predKey){this.predKey=key;this.preview=predict(w,seat,p.stone,power,{path:assist||this.arc});}else if(p.charge<0)this.preview=null;\n }\n event(e){const E=this.E,g=this.game,w=this.world;\n if(e.type==='\"'fall'){const r=E.rng(e.id*177+e.tick);this.debris.push({...e,x:e.x+e.w/2,z:e.z+e.h/2,vx:(r()-.5)*55,vz:25+r()*55,rot:0,spin:(r()-.5)*5,life:2+r(),color:e.material==='W'?'#b28c60':w.courtDef.stone});}\n if(e.type==='hit'){this.flashes.push({...e,life:.22});g.particles.impact(e.x,0,e.z,e.stone===1?1.5:.8,e.kind==='castle'?'#f4d6a2':TEAM[e.seat].color);g.particles.bits(e.x,0,e.z,this.reduced?3:12,[w.courtDef.stone,'#e8d2a3','#665c58']);if(\"'!this.reduced)g.shake(e.stone===1?2:1);}\n if(e.type==='\"'collapse'){if(\"'!this.reduced)g.shake(Math.min(4,e.count*.35));}\n if(e.type==='\"'launch')g.particles.dust(e.x,0,ARENA.ground,5);\n if(e.type==='split')g.particles.glints(e.x,0,e.z,8,STONES[2].color);\n if(e.type==='water'){this.ripples.push({...e,life:1.3});for(let i=0;i<(this.reduced?4:16);i++)g.particles.add({kind:'bit',x:e.x,y:0,z:ARENA.water+2,vx:(i-8)*5,vz:45+(i%4)*15,g:180,max:.6,color:'#b2e5e3',size:1});}\n }\n draw(r){const w=this.world;if(\"'!w)return;const E=this.E,px=E.px,c=w.courtDef,t=this.game.time;\n this.bg.draw(r);\n // A distant tournament pavilion and spectators, behind the lake.\n r.queue(480,22,22,g=>{const P=(x,z)=>r.w(x,22,z);px.poly(g,[P(320,30),P(640,30),P(625,42),P(335,42)],'\"'#6d655f');\n for(let i=0;i<9;i++){const x=340+i*35;px.poly(g,[P(x-19,63),P(x,83),P(x+19,63)],i%2?'#b45e5e':'#d4bb8e');px.line(g,...P(x-18,63),...P(x-18,34),'#66524b',2);}\n for(let x=330;x<=630;x+=10)px.rect(g,...P(x,32),1,8,'#514d4c');});\n this.spectators.forEach(rig=>r.actor(rig.x,rig.y,rig.z,(g,x,y)=>rig.draw(g,x,y,r.view)));\n // Water is cosmetic; its one collision plane lives in the simulation.\n const [wx,wy]=r.w(300,0,ARENA.water),[ex]=r.w(660,0,ARENA.water);r.overlay(g=>{const [,,]=[0,0];px.rect(g,wx,wy,ex-wx,r.H-wy,'#365e74');\n for(let y=0;y<110;y+=4){const a=.35-y/400,col=E.mix('#658a91','#2c4d68',y/130);for(let i=0;i<14;i++){const x=wx+(i*37+Math.sin(t*.6+y)*12+y*4)%(ex-wx);px.rect(g,x,wy+y,9+(i*7+y)%29,1,col);}}\n for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const x=wx+26+i*53;px.rect(g,x+Math.sin(t+i)*5,wy+10+(i%3)*8,14,2,c.id===3?'#ac8a7a':'#92b3ac');}\n for(const e of this.ripples){const q=r.w(e.x,0,ARENA.water),rad=(1.3-e.life)*24;px.ell(g,q[0],q[1]+2,rad,Math.max(1,rad*.15),'#9ec7c2');px.ell(g,q[0],q[1]+2,Math.max(0,rad-2),Math.max(0,rad*.15-1),'#365e74');}});\n this.land.draw(r);\n for(const x of [28,282,678,932]){r.shape('barrel',x,5,ARENA.ground,{scale:.7});r.prop(c.id===3?'brazier':'torch',x,3,ARENA.ground,{size:.9,light:true});}\n for(const x of [15,294,666,945]){r.shape('grass',x,0,ARENA.ground,{params:{h:8,n:6}});}\n for(let seat=0;seat<2;seat++){\n  const blocks=w.castles[seat];for(const b of blocks){if(\"'!b.foundation&&b.hp<=0)continue;\n   r.shape(b.material==='\"'W'?'siegeTimber':'siegeBlock',b.x+b.w/2,-1,b.z,{params:{w:b.w,h:b.h},mats:{s:b.material==='W'?'oak':\"'`siegeStone${c.id}`},shadow:false});\n   r.queue(b.x,0,b.z,g=>{const [x,y]=r.w(b.x,0,b.z+b.h),k=r.ppu;\n    if(!b.foundation){px.rect(g,x+1,y,b.w*k-2,2, b.material==='\"'W'?'#dbc08b':E.tones(c.stone).hi);\n     if(b.material==='R'){px.rect(g,x+3,y+4,2,b.h*k-8,'#687286');px.rect(g,x+b.w*k-5,y+4,2,b.h*k-8,'#687286');}\n     if(b.hp<b.max){px.line(g,x+b.w*k*.6,y+3,x+b.w*k*.42,y+b.h*k*.6,'#4b4950');px.line(g,x+b.w*k*.42,y+b.h*k*.6,x+b.w*k*.66,y+b.h*k-1,'#4b4950');}\n     if(b.h>=17&&b.id%4===0){const sx=x+b.w*k*.45;px.rect(g,sx,y+6,3*k,6*k,'#525967');px.rect(g,sx,y+6,1,6*k,'#d3c3a5');}\n    }\n    if(this.debug){px.rect(g,x,y,b.w*k,1,'#8effca');px.rect(g,x,y,1,b.h*k,'#8effca');for(const id of b.support){const a=blocks.find(q=>q.id===id);if(a&&(a.hp>0||a.foundation))px.line(g,...r.w(b.x+b.w/2,0,b.z+b.h/2),...r.w(a.x+a.w/2,0,a.z+a.h/2),'#b5e9ad');}}\n    if(this.selection?.id===b.id&&seat===0){px.rect(g,x-2,y-2,b.w*k+4,2,'#fff7ad');px.rect(g,x-2,y-2,2,b.h*k+4,'#fff7ad');}\n   });\n  }\n  // Standards attach only to surviving objective blocks.\n  const highest=blocks.filter(b=>\"'!b.foundation&&b.hp>0).sort((a,b)=>b.z+b.h-a.z-a.h)[0];if(highest){const x=highest.x+highest.w/2,z=highest.z+highest.h;\n   r.queue(x,-2,z,g=>{const P=(dx,dz)=>r.w(x+dx,-2,z+dz),a=Math.sin(t*3+seat)*2;px.line(g,...P(0,0),...P(0,34),'\"'#7b6149',2);px.poly(g,[P(1,33),P(24,31+a),P(20,22+a),P(1,23)],TEAM[seat].dark);px.poly(g,[P(2,32),P(22,30+a),P(18,24+a),P(2,24)],TEAM[seat].color);px.disc(g,...P(10,28),2,'#f2d9a3');});}\n  this.catapult(r,seat);\n  for(const rig of this.crews[seat]){r.shadow(rig.x,0,7,.25,undefined,ARENA.ground);r.actor(rig.x,rig.y,rig.z,(g,x,y)=>rig.draw(g,x,y,r.view));}\n  const p=w.players[seat],protectedNow=w.tick>=Math.max(p.crewUntil,p.launcherUntil)&&w.tick<p.protectUntil;\n  if(protectedNow)r.queue(ARENA.launch[seat],0,ARENA.ground,g=>{const P=(x,z)=>r.w(x,0,z);for(const x of [ARENA.launch[seat],ARENA.crew[seat]]){const q=P(x,ARENA.ground+48);px.poly(g,[[q[0]-7,q[1]-4],[q[0]+7,q[1]-4],[q[0]+6,q[1]+4],[q[0],q[1]+10],[q[0]-6,q[1]+4]],'#e9c36b');px.line(g,q[0]-3,q[1]+1,q[0],q[1]+5,'#71563f',2);px.line(g,q[0],q[1]+5,q[0]+4,q[1]-1,'#71563f',2);}});\n  if(w.outcome&&w.outcome.winner\"'!==seat)r.queue(ARENA.crew[seat],0,ARENA.ground,g=>{const q=r.w(ARENA.crew[seat],0,ARENA.ground+44);px.line(g,q[0],q[1]+28,q[0],q[1],'\"'#7c6957',2);px.poly(g,[[q[0],q[1]],[q[0]+22,q[1]+Math.sin(t*3)*2],[q[0]+19,q[1]+13],[q[0],q[1]+12]],'#f5ead2');});\n }\n for(const s of w.shots)r.queue(s.x,0,s.z,g=>{const q=r.w(s.x,0,s.z),k=r.ppu,st=STONES[s.stone],rad=(s.fragment?2.4:st.radius)*k;\n  const speed=Math.hypot(s.vx,s.vz)||1;for(let i=1;i<5;i++)px.disc(g,q[0]-s.vx/speed*i*4,q[1]+s.vz/speed*i*4,Math.max(.6,rad*(1-i*.18)),E.mix(st.color,'#8e9f9b',i/5));\n  px.disc(g,...q,rad+1,'#354256');px.disc(g,...q,rad,st.color);px.disc(g,q[0]-rad*.3,q[1]-rad*.4,Math.max(1,rad*.4),'#fff1cf');if(s.stone===2)px.line(g,q[0],q[1]-rad,q[0]-1,q[1]+rad,'#6c568b');});\n for(const d of this.debris)r.queue(d.x,0,d.z,g=>{const q=r.w(d.x,0,d.z),s=Math.min(8,d.w*.35)*r.ppu,c=Math.cos(d.rot),a=Math.sin(d.rot);px.poly(g,[[-s,-s],[s,-s],[s,s],[-s,s]].map(([x,y])=>[q[0]+x*c-y*a,q[1]+x*a+y*c]),d.color);px.line(g,q[0]-s/2,q[1]-s/2,q[0]+s/2,q[1]-s/2,'#e2ceb0');});\n for(let seat=0;seat<2;seat++){const p=w.players[seat],m=p.last[p.stone];if(m)r.queue(m.x,0,m.z,g=>{const q=r.w(m.x,0,m.z);px.line(g,q[0]-5,q[1]-5,q[0]+5,q[1]+5,TEAM[seat].color);px.line(g,q[0]+5,q[1]-5,q[0]-5,q[1]+5,TEAM[seat].color);});}\n if(this.preview){r.overlay(g=>{for(let i=0;i<this.preview.points.length;i++){const p=this.preview.points[i];px.disc(g,...r.w(p[0],0,p[1]),1,'#f6e9b0');}for(const h of this.preview.hits){const q=r.w(h.x,0,h.z),col=h.kind==='castle'?'#fff0b1':h.kind==='crew'||h.kind==='launcher'?'#f8bb83':'#e5d8ae';px.poly(g,[[q[0],q[1]-7],[q[0]+6,q[1]],[q[0],q[1]+7],[q[0]-6,q[1]]],col);px.disc(g,...q,2,'#41566b');}});}\n }\n catapult(r,seat){const w=this.world,p=w.players[seat],px=this.E.px,dir=seat?-1:1,power=powerOf(w,p),age=(w.tick-p.launchTick)*DT,repair=w.tick<p.launcherUntil,missing=repair?clamp((p.launcherUntil-w.tick)*DT,0,1):0;\n const x=ARENA.launch[seat]+(seat?1:-1)*missing*19,z=ARENA.ground;\n r.shadow(x,0,21,.3,undefined,z);\n r.queue(x,0,z,g=>{const P=(dx,dz)=>r.w(x+dx*dir,0,z+dz),k=r.ppu;\n const beam=(a,b,width,base,edge)=>{px.line(g,...P(...a),...P(...b),'#34333d',width*k+2);px.line(g,...P(...a),...P(...b),base,width*k);px.line(g,...P(a[0]-.5,a[1]+1),...P(b[0]-.5,b[1]+1),edge,Math.max(1,k));};\n beam([-23,6],[23,6],6,'#936844','#d0a36b');beam([-13,8],[0,31],5,'#8b6545','#d0a36b');beam([14,8],[0,31],5,'#8b6545','#c69b65');\n const release=age>=0&&age<.24,rest=-.12,angle=release?(-1.28+age*5):p.charge>=0?-.12+power*1.05:p.ready>w.tick?-.45+clamp((p.ready-w.tick)*DT,0,1)*.5:rest;\n const end=[Math.cos(angle)*-31,25+Math.sin(angle)*-31],tail=[Math.cos(angle)*15,25+Math.sin(angle)*15];beam(tail,end,4,'#a5784c','#edd19a');\n const cord=P(...end),anchor=P(-19,9);px.line(g,...cord,...anchor,'#eadbb0',1);\n px.disc(g,...P(...end),5*k,'#453a3b');px.disc(g,...P(end[0],end[1]+1),3*k,'#b6a17e');if(age>.22&&p.ready<=w.tick)px.disc(g,...P(end[0],end[1]+2),3*k,STONES[p.stone].color);\n for(const wx of [-17,17]){const q=P(wx,4);px.disc(g,...q,7*k,'#2e3540');px.disc(g,...q,5.5*k,'#a57d50');for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const a=i*Math.PI/3+(p.charge>=0?power*9:0);px.line(g,q[0],q[1],q[0]+Math.cos(a)*5*k,q[1]+Math.sin(a)*5*k,'#e3bb7d',k);}px.disc(g,...q,2*k,'#4f5055');}\n px.disc(g,...P(0,26),4*k,'#a8b5bf');px.disc(g,...P(0,26),2*k,'#4a4d5a');\n const q=P(0,13);px.poly(g,[[q[0]-7*k,q[1]-4*k],[q[0]+7*k,q[1]-4*k],[q[0]+5*k,q[1]+5*k],[q[0],q[1]+8*k],[q[0]-5*k,q[1]+5*k]],TEAM[seat].color);px.disc(g,q[0],q[1],2*k,'#ffe7ab');\n if(repair){const q=P(0,48);this.E.font.text(g,'REPAIR',...q,'#ffe0b0',{align:'center',outline:false});}\n });}\n}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/content.js'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"'....W..W.W'\\\",\\\"'....W..W'\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > src/audio.js <<'EOF'\n// Every sound is synthesized. Native music/effects/voice buses own the user's gain exactly once.\nexport function formant(ctx,bus,time,freq=190,duration=.13,vol=.055,index=0) {\n const osc=ctx.createOscillator(),filter=ctx.createBiquadFilter(),gain=ctx.createGain();\n osc.type='sawtooth';osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq,time);osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(freq*(index%2?1.35:.8),time+duration);\n filter.type='bandpass';filter.frequency.value=[780,1200,1700,950][index%4];filter.Q.value=4;\n gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0,time);gain.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol,time+.012);gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,time+duration);\n osc.connect(filter).connect(gain).connect(bus);osc.start(time);osc.stop(time+duration+.02);osc.onended=()=>{osc.disconnect();filter.disconnect();gain.disconnect();};return osc;\n}\nexport function lute(ctx,bus,time,freq,dur,vol) {\n const osc=ctx.createOscillator(),g=ctx.createGain(),f=ctx.createBiquadFilter();osc.type='triangle';osc.frequency.value=freq;f.type='lowpass';f.frequency.setValueAtTime(3500,time);f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(500,time+Math.max(.04,dur));\n g.gain.setValueAtTime(0,time);g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol,time+.004);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,time+Math.max(.04,dur));osc.connect(f).connect(g).connect(bus);osc.start(time);osc.stop(time+dur+.04);osc.onended=()=>{osc.disconnect();f.disconnect();g.disconnect();};\n}\nexport const MARCH = {bpm:104,steps:4,tracks:[\n {wave:'siegeLute',vol:.13,notes:'D4 . A4 . D5 - C5 . B4 . A4 . G4 . E4 . | F4 . A4 . D5 . F5 - E5 . D5 . C5 . A4 . | G4 . B4 . E5 . D5 . C5 . A4 . F4 . E4 . | D4 . F4 . A4 . D5 - A4 . F4 . D4 - . .'},\n {wave:'triangle',vol:.12,notes:'D3 . . . A2 . . . D3 . . . A2 . . . | F3 . . . C3 . . . F3 . . . A2 . . . | G2 . . . D3 . . . A2 . . . A2 . . . | D3 . . . A2 . . . D3 . . . D3 . . .'},\n {wave:'drums',vol:.045,notes:'k . . h . . s . k . h . s . . h'}]};\nexport class SiegeAudio {\n constructor(game){this.game=game;this.lastVoice=-100;this.voices=[];this.ended=false;const a=game.audio;a.instrument('siegeLute',lute);\n const patches={\n siegeWind:{wave:'noise',freq:260,to:450,dur:.06,vol:.06},siegeLaunch:[{wave:'noise',freq:650,to:130,dur:.17,vol:.12},{wave:'triangle',freq:95,to:45,dur:.13,vol:.13}],\n siegeStone:[{wave:'noise',freq:950,to:110,dur:.24,vol:.12},{wave:'sine',freq:130,to:45,dur:.2,vol:.15}],\n siegeWood:{wave:'noise',freq:1700,to:300,dur:.17,vol:.14},siegeCrew:{wave:'triangle',freq:440,to:230,dur:.16,vol:.10},\n siegeArmor:[{wave:'square',freq:180,to:75,dur:.12,vol:.07},{wave:'sine',freq:840,to:420,dur:.24,vol:.06}],\n siegeWater:{wave:'sine',freq:320,to:70,dur:.24,vol:.14},siegeRepair:{wave:'triangle',freq:370,to:210,dur:.045,vol:.09},\n siegeReturn:{wave:'triangle',freq:440,arp:[0,4,7,12],step:.06,dur:.26,vol:.10},siegeCancel:{wave:'sine',freq:240,to:140,dur:.09,vol:.06}};\n for(const k in patches)a.define(k,patches[k]);}\n music(court=0){if(this.ended)return;const song={...MARCH,bpm:[104,96,112,86,123][court],tracks:MARCH.tracks};this.game.audio.music(song,{sync:true});}\n voice(variant=0){if(this.ended||this.game.real-this.lastVoice<3)return;this.lastVoice=this.game.real;const a=this.game.audio,bus=a.bus('voice'),ctx=a.ctx;if(\"'!ctx||!bus||ctx.state!=='\"'running')return;\n for(let i=0;i<4;i++)this.voices.push(formant(ctx,bus,ctx.currentTime+i*.105,variant?145+i*13:210-i*15,.1,.09,i+variant));this.voices=this.voices.filter(o=>o.context.currentTime<o.context.currentTime+1).slice(-20);}\n event(e){if(this.ended)return;const a=this.game.audio;if(e.type==='launch')a.sfx('siegeLaunch',{pitch:e.stone===1?.72:1});\n else if(e.type==='wind')a.sfx('siegeWind');else if(e.type==='cancel')a.sfx('siegeCancel');\n else if(e.type==='water')a.sfx('siegeWater');else if(e.type==='recovery')a.sfx('siegeReturn');\n else if(e.type==='hit'){a.sfx(e.kind==='crew'?'siegeCrew':e.kind==='launcher'?'siegeArmor':'siegeStone');if(e.kind\"'!=='\"'castle')this.voice(e.seat);}\n else if(e.type==='collapse'){a.sfx('siegeWood',{pitch:.7});this.voice(1);}\n else if(e.type==='split')a.sfx('whoosh',{vol:.25,pitch:1.4});else if(e.type==='outcome'){this.fanfare(e.winner);this.voice(1);}}\n fanfare(winner){this.game.audio.sting({bpm:136,steps:4,tracks:[{wave:'triangle',vol:.18,notes:winner<0?'D4 - F4 - E4 - D4 -':'D4 . D4 . A4 - F#4 - A4 - D5 - - - - -'},{wave:'siegeLute',vol:.10,notes:'D3 - A3 - D4 - - - D3 - A3 - D4 - - -'}]});}\n reset(){for(const v of this.voices)try{v.stop();}catch{}this.voices=[];this.lastVoice=-100;this.game.audio.stopMusic(0);}\n stop(){this.reset();this.ended=true;this.game.audio.mute(true);try{this.game.audio.ctx?.suspend()?.catch(()=>{});}catch{}}\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/view.js <<'EOF'\nimport { ARENA, STONES, DT, clamp } from './config.js';\nimport { COURTS } from './content.js';\nimport { powerOf, predict, remaining, readyAt } from './sim.js';\nexport const TEAM = [{color:'#75dfd4',dark:'#245e64',name:'THE TEAL TROUPE'},{color:'#ff9c75',dark:'#843e4b',name:'THE CORAL COURT'}];\nexport class Battlefield {\n constructor(game,E){this.game=game;this.E=E;this.world=null;this.debris=[];this.ripples=[];this.flashes=[];this.poses=[];this.guidance=[800,160];this.debug=false;this.arc=false;this.selection=null;this.preview=null;\n E.VIEWS.siege=new E.View('siege','Tournament',0,0,1,1);\n for(const c of COURTS)E.MATERIALS[\"'`siegeStone${c.id}`]={color:c.stone,pattern:'\"'stones',size:6,over:[['cracks'],['moss','#68805c',{amount:.15}]]};\n E.SHAPES.siegeBlock={about:'An individually destructible tournament ashlar',mats:{s:'stone'},params:{w:19,h:18},make:p=>[['box','s',[0,0,0],[p.w,11,p.h]]]};\n E.SHAPES.siegeTimber={about:'Braced timber tower section',mats:{s:'oak',b:'walnut'},params:{w:19,h:18},make:p=>[['box','s',[0,0,0],[p.w,11,p.h]],['box','b',[0,6,0],[2,1,p.h]],['box','b',[0,6,p.h-3],[p.w,1,2]]]};\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeHaul',(J,w,rig)=>{const t=rig.t*12;for(const [id,phase]of[['handR',0],['handL',Math.PI]]){J[id][0]+=(8+Math.cos(t+phase)*3-J[id][0])*w;J[id][2]+=(17+Math.sin(t+phase)*3-J[id][2])*w;}J.head[0]+=3*w;});\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeTools',(J,w,rig)=>{J.handR[0]+=(9-J.handR[0])*w;J.handR[2]+=(12+Math.sin(rig.t*16)*5-J.handR[2])*w;J.handL[2]+=(17-J.handL[2])*w;});\n E.Humanoid.pose('siegeFlag',(J,w)=>{J.handR[0]+=(8-J.handR[0])*w;J.handR[2]+=(26-J.handR[2])*w;});\n this.crews=[0,1].map(seat=>[0,1].map(i=>new E.Humanoid({size:.86,build:i?'bulky':'heroic',outfit:'tunic',hat:i?'band':'helmet',weapon:null,sleeves:'long',hair:i?'short':'spiky',seed:seat*20+i+4,colors:{cloth:TEAM[seat].color,pants:'#333e56',hair:i?'#b9844f':'#e8c17c',trim:'#eed7a1',skin:i?'#c69a78':'#e7bfa0',metal:'#9babc0',boot:'#352c35'}})));\n this.spectators=Array.from({length:15},(_,i)=>new E.Humanoid({size:.58,hat:i%3?'cap':'crown',outfit:i%2?'robe':'tunic',weapon:null,seed:40+i,colors:{cloth:['#8d4857','#69775a','#9a8553','#567e8b'][i%4],trim:'#c5ac72',skin:i%3?'#d8ae8b':'#a67c65'}}));\n }\n reset(w){this.world=w;this.debris=[];this.ripples=[];this.flashes=[];this.preview=null;this.predKey='';const c=w.courtDef;\n this.bg=new this.E.Backdrop({sky:c.id===3?['#111a3b','#465175','#ba7d79']:c.id===0?['#668ba2','#aac0b9','#e4d2aa']:['#3f506e','#9d8b8d','#ebc49c'],sun:c.id===3?undefined:{x:.52,y:.28,r:25,color:'#f4d9a7'},moon:c.id===3?{x:.53,y:.24,r:20,color:'#ece0b8'}:undefined,stars:c.id===3?60:0,layers:[{kind:'mountains',color:c.id===3?'#28334d':'#8c9699',y:.50,height:.20,parallax:.1},{kind:'castle',color:c.id===3?'#354157':'#a3a795',y:.66,height:.13,parallax:.2},{kind:'clouds',color:c.id===3?'#58526e':'#dfd4bd',y:.18,height:.13,parallax:.3,drift:2},{kind:'hills',color:c.id===3?'#324853':'#869780',y:.74,height:.14,parallax:.4}]});\n this.land=new this.E.Terrain({w:960,h:70,y:-34,materials:[{color:c.id===1?'#9c8865':'#777061',top:c.grass,edge:'#343a41',depth:5},{color:'#4f535a',top:'#71767a',edge:'#30343d',depth:3}],chunk:64});\n this.land.fill((x,z)=>x<307||x>653?z<ARENA.ground?(z<13?2:1):0:0);\n this.game.lights.enabled=true;this.game.lights.ambient=c.id===3?.7:.92;\n this.game.particles.ground=(x,y,z)=>x<307||x>653?ARENA.ground:ARENA.water;\n }\n update(dt,{seat=0,assist=false,reduced=false,title=false}={}){const w=this.world;if(\"'!w)return;this.reduced=reduced;const g=this.game;\n // Fit the whole lane. Portrait leaves room for a readable target inset above it.\n const ppu=Math.min(g.W/1000,g.H/440);g.view.zoom=ppu;g.view._siegeZoom=ppu; // View axes are refreshed via setZoom below when changed.\n if(Math.abs((g.zoom||1)-ppu)>.003){g.setZoom(ppu);}\n g.cam.smooth=0;g.cam.bounds=null;g.focus(480,0,130);\n for(let s=0;s<2;s++){const p=w.players[s],end=Math.max(p.crewUntil,p.launcherUntil),missing=w.tick<end,retreat=missing?clamp((end-w.tick)*DT*2,0,1):0;\n this.crews[s].forEach((rig,i)=>{const repair=w.tick<p.launcherUntil,charge=p.charge>=0,win=w.outcome?.winner===s;\n const x=ARENA.crew[s]+(s?-1:1)*(i?-17:0)+(s?1:-1)*retreat*28;\n const pose=w.outcome?(win?'\"'cheer':'siegeFlag'):missing?(repair?'siegeTools':'down'):charge?'siegeHaul':'hips';\n rig.update(dt,{x,y:i?4:0,z:ARENA.ground,facing:s?Math.PI:0,pose,expr:missing?'wince':win?'smile':charge?'angry':null,run:retreat>0?.8:0});});}\n this.spectators.forEach((rig,i)=>rig.update(dt,{x:340+i*20,y:15,z:30,facing:i%2?0:Math.PI,pose:w.outcome?'cheer':i%4===0?'wave':'hips'}));\n for(const d of this.debris){d.life-=dt;d.vz-=300*dt;d.x+=d.vx*dt;d.z+=d.vz*dt;d.rot+=dt*d.spin;if(d.z<ARENA.water&&d.life>.35)d.life=.35;}\n this.debris=this.debris.filter(d=>d.life>0);this.ripples=this.ripples.filter(d=>(d.life-=dt)>0);this.flashes=this.flashes.filter(d=>(d.life-=dt)>0);\n const p=w.players[seat],power=powerOf(w,p),key=[w.revision,p.stone,Math.round(power*150),assist].join(':');\n if(p.charge>=0&&key\"'!==this.predKey){this.predKey=key;this.preview=predict(w,seat,p.stone,power,{path:assist||this.arc});}else if(p.charge<0)this.preview=null;\n }\n event(e){const E=this.E,g=this.game,w=this.world;\n if(e.type==='\"'fall'){const r=E.rng(e.id*177+e.tick);this.debris.push({...e,x:e.x+e.w/2,z:e.z+e.h/2,vx:(r()-.5)*55,vz:25+r()*55,rot:0,spin:(r()-.5)*5,life:2+r(),color:e.material==='W'?'#b28c60':w.courtDef.stone});}\n if(e.type==='hit'){this.flashes.push({...e,life:.22});g.particles.impact(e.x,0,e.z,e.stone===1?1.5:.8,e.kind==='castle'?'#f4d6a2':TEAM[e.seat].color);g.particles.bits(e.x,0,e.z,this.reduced?3:12,[w.courtDef.stone,'#e8d2a3','#665c58']);if(\"'!this.reduced)g.shake(e.stone===1?2:1);}\n if(e.type==='\"'collapse'){if(\"'!this.reduced)g.shake(Math.min(4,e.count*.35));}\n if(e.type==='\"'launch')g.particles.dust(e.x,0,ARENA.ground,5);\n if(e.type==='split')g.particles.glints(e.x,0,e.z,8,STONES[2].color);\n if(e.type==='water'){this.ripples.push({...e,life:1.3});for(let i=0;i<(this.reduced?4:16);i++)g.particles.add({kind:'bit',x:e.x,y:0,z:ARENA.water+2,vx:(i-8)*5,vz:45+(i%4)*15,g:180,max:.6,color:'#b2e5e3',size:1});}\n }\n draw(r){const w=this.world;if(\"'!w)return;const E=this.E,px=E.px,c=w.courtDef,t=this.game.time;\n this.bg.draw(r);\n // A distant tournament pavilion and spectators, behind the lake.\n r.queue(480,22,22,g=>{const P=(x,z)=>r.w(x,22,z);px.poly(g,[P(320,30),P(640,30),P(625,42),P(335,42)],'\"'#6d655f');\n for(let i=0;i<9;i++){const x=340+i*35;px.poly(g,[P(x-19,63),P(x,83),P(x+19,63)],i%2?'#b45e5e':'#d4bb8e');px.line(g,...P(x-18,63),...P(x-18,34),'#66524b',2);}\n for(let x=330;x<=630;x+=10)px.rect(g,...P(x,32),1,8,'#514d4c');});\n this.spectators.forEach(rig=>r.actor(rig.x,rig.y,rig.z,(g,x,y)=>rig.draw(g,x,y,r.view)));\n // Water is cosmetic; its one collision plane lives in the simulation.\n const [wx,wy]=r.w(300,0,ARENA.water),[ex]=r.w(660,0,ARENA.water);r.overlay(g=>{const [,,]=[0,0];px.rect(g,wx,wy,ex-wx,r.H-wy,'#365e74');\n for(let y=0;y<110;y+=4){const a=.35-y/400,col=E.mix('#658a91','#2c4d68',y/130);for(let i=0;i<14;i++){const x=wx+(i*37+Math.sin(t*.6+y)*12+y*4)%(ex-wx);px.rect(g,x,wy+y,9+(i*7+y)%29,1,col);}}\n for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const x=wx+26+i*53;px.rect(g,x+Math.sin(t+i)*5,wy+10+(i%3)*8,14,2,c.id===3?'#ac8a7a':'#92b3ac');}\n for(const e of this.ripples){const q=r.w(e.x,0,ARENA.water),rad=(1.3-e.life)*24;px.ell(g,q[0],q[1]+2,rad,Math.max(1,rad*.15),'#9ec7c2');px.ell(g,q[0],q[1]+2,Math.max(0,rad-2),Math.max(0,rad*.15-1),'#365e74');}});\n this.land.draw(r);\n for(const x of [28,282,678,932]){r.shape('barrel',x,5,ARENA.ground,{scale:.7});r.prop(c.id===3?'brazier':'torch',x,3,ARENA.ground,{size:.9,light:true});}\n for(const x of [15,294,666,945]){r.shape('grass',x,0,ARENA.ground,{params:{h:8,n:6}});}\n for(let seat=0;seat<2;seat++){\n  const blocks=w.castles[seat];for(const b of blocks){if(\"'!b.foundation&&b.hp<=0)continue;\n   r.shape(b.material==='\"'W'?'siegeTimber':'siegeBlock',b.x+b.w/2,-1,b.z,{params:{w:b.w,h:b.h},mats:{s:b.material==='W'?'oak':\"'`siegeStone${c.id}`},shadow:false});\n   r.queue(b.x,0,b.z,g=>{const [x,y]=r.w(b.x,0,b.z+b.h),k=r.ppu;\n    if(!b.foundation){px.rect(g,x+1,y,b.w*k-2,2, b.material==='\"'W'?'#dbc08b':E.tones(c.stone).hi);\n     if(b.material==='R'){px.rect(g,x+3,y+4,2,b.h*k-8,'#687286');px.rect(g,x+b.w*k-5,y+4,2,b.h*k-8,'#687286');}\n     if(b.hp<b.max){px.line(g,x+b.w*k*.6,y+3,x+b.w*k*.42,y+b.h*k*.6,'#4b4950');px.line(g,x+b.w*k*.42,y+b.h*k*.6,x+b.w*k*.66,y+b.h*k-1,'#4b4950');}\n     if(b.h>=17&&b.id%4===0){const sx=x+b.w*k*.45;px.rect(g,sx,y+6,3*k,6*k,'#525967');px.rect(g,sx,y+6,1,6*k,'#d3c3a5');}\n    }\n    if(this.debug){px.rect(g,x,y,b.w*k,1,'#8effca');px.rect(g,x,y,1,b.h*k,'#8effca');for(const id of b.support){const a=blocks.find(q=>q.id===id);if(a&&(a.hp>0||a.foundation))px.line(g,...r.w(b.x+b.w/2,0,b.z+b.h/2),...r.w(a.x+a.w/2,0,a.z+a.h/2),'#b5e9ad');}}\n    if(this.selection?.id===b.id&&seat===0){px.rect(g,x-2,y-2,b.w*k+4,2,'#fff7ad');px.rect(g,x-2,y-2,2,b.h*k+4,'#fff7ad');}\n   });\n  }\n  // Standards attach only to surviving objective blocks.\n  const highest=blocks.filter(b=>\"'!b.foundation&&b.hp>0).sort((a,b)=>b.z+b.h-a.z-a.h)[0];if(highest){const x=highest.x+highest.w/2,z=highest.z+highest.h;\n   r.queue(x,-2,z,g=>{const P=(dx,dz)=>r.w(x+dx,-2,z+dz),a=Math.sin(t*3+seat)*2;px.line(g,...P(0,0),...P(0,34),'\"'#7b6149',2);px.poly(g,[P(1,33),P(24,31+a),P(20,22+a),P(1,23)],TEAM[seat].dark);px.poly(g,[P(2,32),P(22,30+a),P(18,24+a),P(2,24)],TEAM[seat].color);px.disc(g,...P(10,28),2,'#f2d9a3');});}\n  this.catapult(r,seat);\n  for(const rig of this.crews[seat]){r.shadow(rig.x,0,7,.25,undefined,ARENA.ground);r.actor(rig.x,rig.y,rig.z,(g,x,y)=>rig.draw(g,x,y,r.view));}\n  const p=w.players[seat],protectedNow=w.tick>=Math.max(p.crewUntil,p.launcherUntil)&&w.tick<p.protectUntil;\n  if(protectedNow)r.queue(ARENA.launch[seat],0,ARENA.ground,g=>{const P=(x,z)=>r.w(x,0,z);for(const x of [ARENA.launch[seat],ARENA.crew[seat]]){const q=P(x,ARENA.ground+48);px.poly(g,[[q[0]-7,q[1]-4],[q[0]+7,q[1]-4],[q[0]+6,q[1]+4],[q[0],q[1]+10],[q[0]-6,q[1]+4]],'#e9c36b');px.line(g,q[0]-3,q[1]+1,q[0],q[1]+5,'#71563f',2);px.line(g,q[0],q[1]+5,q[0]+4,q[1]-1,'#71563f',2);}});\n  if(w.outcome&&w.outcome.winner\"'!==seat)r.queue(ARENA.crew[seat],0,ARENA.ground,g=>{const q=r.w(ARENA.crew[seat],0,ARENA.ground+44);px.line(g,q[0],q[1]+28,q[0],q[1],'\"'#7c6957',2);px.poly(g,[[q[0],q[1]],[q[0]+22,q[1]+Math.sin(t*3)*2],[q[0]+19,q[1]+13],[q[0],q[1]+12]],'#f5ead2');});\n }\n for(const s of w.shots)r.queue(s.x,0,s.z,g=>{const q=r.w(s.x,0,s.z),k=r.ppu,st=STONES[s.stone],rad=(s.fragment?2.4:st.radius)*k;\n  const speed=Math.hypot(s.vx,s.vz)||1;for(let i=1;i<5;i++)px.disc(g,q[0]-s.vx/speed*i*4,q[1]+s.vz/speed*i*4,Math.max(.6,rad*(1-i*.18)),E.mix(st.color,'#8e9f9b',i/5));\n  px.disc(g,...q,rad+1,'#354256');px.disc(g,...q,rad,st.color);px.disc(g,q[0]-rad*.3,q[1]-rad*.4,Math.max(1,rad*.4),'#fff1cf');if(s.stone===2)px.line(g,q[0],q[1]-rad,q[0]-1,q[1]+rad,'#6c568b');});\n for(const d of this.debris)r.queue(d.x,0,d.z,g=>{const q=r.w(d.x,0,d.z),s=Math.min(8,d.w*.35)*r.ppu,c=Math.cos(d.rot),a=Math.sin(d.rot);px.poly(g,[[-s,-s],[s,-s],[s,s],[-s,s]].map(([x,y])=>[q[0]+x*c-y*a,q[1]+x*a+y*c]),d.color);px.line(g,q[0]-s/2,q[1]-s/2,q[0]+s/2,q[1]-s/2,'#e2ceb0');});\n for(let seat=0;seat<2;seat++){const p=w.players[seat],m=p.last[p.stone];if(m)r.queue(m.x,0,m.z,g=>{const q=r.w(m.x,0,m.z);px.line(g,q[0]-5,q[1]-5,q[0]+5,q[1]+5,TEAM[seat].color);px.line(g,q[0]+5,q[1]-5,q[0]-5,q[1]+5,TEAM[seat].color);});}\n if(this.preview){r.overlay(g=>{for(let i=0;i<this.preview.points.length;i++){const p=this.preview.points[i];px.disc(g,...r.w(p[0],0,p[1]),1,'#f6e9b0');}for(const h of this.preview.hits){const q=r.w(h.x,0,h.z),col=h.kind==='castle'?'#fff0b1':h.kind==='crew'||h.kind==='launcher'?'#f8bb83':'#e5d8ae';px.poly(g,[[q[0],q[1]-7],[q[0]+6,q[1]],[q[0],q[1]+7],[q[0]-6,q[1]]],col);px.disc(g,...q,2,'#41566b');}});}\n }\n catapult(r,seat){const w=this.world,p=w.players[seat],px=this.E.px,dir=seat?-1:1,power=powerOf(w,p),age=(w.tick-p.launchTick)*DT,repair=w.tick<p.launcherUntil,missing=repair?clamp((p.launcherUntil-w.tick)*DT,0,1):0;\n const x=ARENA.launch[seat]+(seat?1:-1)*missing*19,z=ARENA.ground;\n r.shadow(x,0,21,.3,undefined,z);\n r.queue(x,0,z,g=>{const P=(dx,dz)=>r.w(x+dx*dir,0,z+dz),k=r.ppu;\n const beam=(a,b,width,base,edge)=>{px.line(g,...P(...a),...P(...b),'#34333d',width*k+2);px.line(g,...P(...a),...P(...b),base,width*k);px.line(g,...P(a[0]-.5,a[1]+1),...P(b[0]-.5,b[1]+1),edge,Math.max(1,k));};\n beam([-23,6],[23,6],6,'#936844','#d0a36b');beam([-13,8],[0,31],5,'#8b6545','#d0a36b');beam([14,8],[0,31],5,'#8b6545','#c69b65');\n const release=age>=0&&age<.24,rest=-.12,angle=release?(-1.28+age*5):p.charge>=0?-.12+power*1.05:p.ready>w.tick?-.45+clamp((p.ready-w.tick)*DT,0,1)*.5:rest;\n const end=[Math.cos(angle)*-31,25+Math.sin(angle)*-31],tail=[Math.cos(angle)*15,25+Math.sin(angle)*15];beam(tail,end,4,'#a5784c','#edd19a');\n const cord=P(...end),anchor=P(-19,9);px.line(g,...cord,...anchor,'#eadbb0',1);\n px.disc(g,...P(...end),5*k,'#453a3b');px.disc(g,...P(end[0],end[1]+1),3*k,'#b6a17e');if(age>.22&&p.ready<=w.tick)px.disc(g,...P(end[0],end[1]+2),3*k,STONES[p.stone].color);\n for(const wx of [-17,17]){const q=P(wx,4);px.disc(g,...q,7*k,'#2e3540');px.disc(g,...q,5.5*k,'#a57d50');for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const a=i*Math.PI/3+(p.charge>=0?power*9:0);px.line(g,q[0],q[1],q[0]+Math.cos(a)*5*k,q[1]+Math.sin(a)*5*k,'#e3bb7d',k);}px.disc(g,...q,2*k,'#4f5055');}\n px.disc(g,...P(0,26),4*k,'#a8b5bf');px.disc(g,...P(0,26),2*k,'#4a4d5a');\n const q=P(0,13);px.poly(g,[[q[0]-7*k,q[1]-4*k],[q[0]+7*k,q[1]-4*k],[q[0]+5*k,q[1]+5*k],[q[0],q[1]+8*k],[q[0]-5*k,q[1]+5*k]],TEAM[seat].color);px.disc(g,q[0],q[1],2*k,'#ffe7ab');\n if(repair){const q=P(0,48);this.E.font.text(g,'REPAIR',...q,'#ffe0b0',{align:'center',outline:false});}\n });}\n}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/online.js <<'EOF'\nimport { DT, clamp, tickOf } from './config.js';\nimport { createWorld, command, step, finish, pack, unpack, health, cancel } from './sim.js';\nexport class Transport {\n constructor(hub,clock=()=>performance.now()){this.hub=hub;this.clock=clock;this.queue=[];this.tokens=26;this.refill=clock();this.lastSnap=-1000;this.stopped=false;this.metrics={sent:0,bytes:0,retries:0,rejected:0,maxBytes:0,maxSnapshot:0,packets:[]};}\n enqueue(data,options={}){if(this.stopped)return false;let raw;try{raw=JSON.stringify(data);}catch{this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n const bytes=new TextEncoder().encode(raw).length;if(bytes>16000){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n if(this.queue.length>=64){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n this.queue.push({data,options:{reliable:true,...options},bytes});return true;}\n send(data,options={}){const raw=JSON.stringify(data),bytes=new TextEncoder().encode(raw).length;if(bytes>16000){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}return this.trySend({data,options,bytes});}\n trySend(m){if(this.stopped)return false;const now=this.clock();this.tokens=Math.min(26,this.tokens+(now-this.refill)*.014);this.refill=now;\n if(this.tokens<1)return false;\n if(\"'!this.hub.send(m.data,m.options)){this.metrics.retries++;return false;}\n this.tokens--;this.metrics.sent++;this.metrics.bytes+=m.bytes;this.metrics.maxBytes=Math.max(this.metrics.maxBytes,m.bytes);if(m.data.t==='\"'s')this.metrics.maxSnapshot=Math.max(this.metrics.maxSnapshot,m.bytes);\n this.metrics.packets.push([now,m.bytes,m.options.reliable\"'!==false]);if(this.metrics.packets.length>1000)this.metrics.packets.shift();return true;}\n flush(){while(this.queue.length&&this.trySend(this.queue[0]))this.queue.shift();}\n stop(){this.stopped=true;this.queue=[];}\n}\nexport class OnlineMatch {\n constructor(hub,{onWorld,onEnd,onEvent}={}){this.hub=hub;this.onWorld=onWorld;this.onEnd=onEnd;this.onEvent=onEvent;this.info=null;this.world=null;this.transport=new Transport(hub);this.started=false;this.ended=false;this.finished=false;this.seq=0;this.snapSeq=0;this.lastSeq=-1;this.ack=-1;this.lastSnapshot=-1000;this.lastBaseline=-10000;this.lastEvent=0;this.pendingFinish=false;this.intentStart=null;this.localPower=null;this.leavers=new Set();this.beginTimes=new Map();this.unsub=[];}\n async connect(){const info=await this.hub.connect({mode:'\"'shared-world',seats:[2,2]});if(\"'!info)return null;this.info=info;\n this.world=createWorld({mode:'\"'hub',court:4,seed:info.seed||71,duration:Math.min(180,(info.limitMs||180000)/1000)});this.seat=info.server?null:info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===info.me);if(this.seat<0)this.seat=null;\n const on=(event,fn)=>this.unsub.push(this.hub.on(event,fn));\n on('start',()=>{this.started=true;if(info.isHost)this.baseline();});\n on('message',(data,from)=>this.message(data,from));\n on('leave',({id})=>{this.leavers.add(id);const seat=info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===id);if(seat>=0&&info.isHost){cancel(this.world,seat,false);if(this.started&&\"'!this.finished)finish(this.world,'\"'opponent left',1-seat);this.pendingFinish=true;}});\n on('time-up',()=>{if(info.isHost&&\"'!this.finished){finish(this.world,'\"'timeout');this.pendingFinish=true;this.finalize();}});\n on('end',e=>{this.ended=true;this.transport.stop();this.intentStart=null;this.localPower=null;this.onEnd?.(e);});\n this.onWorld?.(this.world);this.hub.ready();return info;}\n intent(kind,stone){if(this.ended||\"'!this.started||this.hub.time()<0||this.seat===null)return false;\n const now=this.hub.time()/1000;const c={kind,seq:++this.seq,at:now};\n if(kind==='\"'stone')c.stone=stone;\n if(kind==='begin')this.intentStart=now;\n if(kind==='release'){c.duration=this.intentStart===null?0:clamp(now-this.intentStart,0,3);this.intentStart=null;}\n if(kind==='cancel')this.intentStart=null;\n if(this.info.isHost)return this.receiveIntent(c,this.info.me);\n return this.transport.enqueue({t:'c',c},{to:this.info.host});}\n receiveIntent(c,from){if(\"'!this.info.isHost||this.ended||!this.started||this.hub.time()<0||!c||typeof c!=='\"'object')return false;\n const seat=this.info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===from);if(seat<0||this.leavers.has(from)||\"'!Number.isSafeInteger(c.seq)||!['\"'begin','release','cancel','stone'].includes(c.kind)||\"'!Number.isFinite(c.at))return false;\n const now=this.hub.time()/1000;if(c.at>now+.25||c.at<now-2.5)return false;\n if(c.kind==='\"'release'&&(\"'!Number.isFinite(c.duration)||c.duration<0||c.duration>3))return false;\n return command(this.world,seat,c);}\n message(m,from){if(this.ended||!m||typeof m!=='\"'object')return;\n if(this.info.isHost){if(m.t==='c')this.receiveIntent(m.c,from);else if(m.t==='ack'&&this.info.players.some(p=>p.id===from)&&Number.isInteger(m.n))this.ack=Math.max(this.ack,m.n);return;}\n if(from\"'!==this.info.host)return;\n if((m.t==='\"'b'||m.t==='s')&&m.v===1&&Number.isInteger(m.n)&&m.n>this.lastSeq){if(unpack(this.world,m)){this.lastSeq=m.n;if(m.t==='b')this.transport.enqueue({t:'ack',n:m.n},{to:this.info.host});}}\n if(m.t==='e'&&Number.isInteger(m.n)&&m.n>(this.eventSeq??-1)){this.eventSeq=m.n;for(const e of m.e||[])this.onEvent?.(e);}\n }\n baseline(){const p=pack(this.world,++this.snapSeq);p.t='b';this.transport.enqueue(p);this.lastBaseline=this.hub.time();}\n update(){if(this.ended||\"'!this.info)return;this.transport.flush();const ms=this.hub.time();if(!this.started||ms<0)return;\n if(this.info.isHost){\n  const target=Math.min(this.world.deadline,Math.floor(ms/1000/DT));let n=0;while(this.world.tick<target&&this.world.phase==='\"'playing'&&n++<600)step(this.world);\n  const events=this.world.events.splice(0);if(events.length){for(const e of events)this.onEvent?.(e);this.transport.enqueue({t:'e',n:++this.lastEvent,e:events.filter(e=>e.type\"'!=='\"'fall'||e.id%2===0)});}\n  if(ms-this.lastBaseline>=2000)this.baseline();\n  if(ms-this.lastSnapshot>=140&&this.transport.queue.length===0){const snap=pack(this.world,++this.snapSeq);if(JSON.stringify(snap).length<=1200){this.transport.send(snap,{reliable:false});}else this.transport.enqueue({...snap,t:'b'});this.lastSnapshot=ms;}\n  if(this.world.outcome&&\"'!this.finished){this.pendingFinish=true;this.finalize();}\n }\n this.transport.flush();}\n finalize(){if(!this.info?.isHost||this.finished||this.ended)return;const w=this.world;if(!w.outcome)finish(w,'\"'timeout');\n if(\"'!this.finalQueued){this.baseline();this.finalQueued=true;}this.transport.flush();if(this.transport.queue.length)return;\n const ids=this.info.players.map(p=>p.id).filter(id=>!this.leavers.has(id)),winner=w.outcome.winner,winid=winner>=0?this.info.players[winner]?.id:null;\n const standings=winner<0?[ids]:[ids.filter(id=>id===winid),ids.filter(id=>id!==winid)].filter(a=>a.length);\n const scores=Object.fromEntries(this.info.players.map((p,i)=>[p.id,Math.round(health(w,i)*1000)+w.players[i].score]));\n this.finished=true;this.hub.finish({standings,scores});this.pendingFinish=false;}\n dispose(){this.ended=true;this.transport.stop();for(const f of this.unsub)f();}\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/persistence.js <<'\"'EOF'\nexport const SAVE_KEY='smithereens-under-siege:tour:v1';\nexport function loadTour(storage){try{const s=JSON.parse(storage.getItem(SAVE_KEY));if(s?.version===1&&Number.isInteger(s.next)&&s.next>=1&&s.next<10&&Number.isInteger(s.seed)&&Array.isArray(s.totals)&&s.totals.length===2&&s.totals.every(n=>Number.isFinite(n)&&n>=0&&n<1e7)&&Array.isArray(s.results)&&s.results.length===s.next)return s;}catch{}return null;}\nexport function saveTour(storage,s){try{storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY,JSON.stringify({version:1,...s}));return true;}catch{return false;}}\nexport function eraseTour(storage){try{storage.removeItem(SAVE_KEY);}catch{}}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/online.js <<'EOF'\nimport { DT, clamp, tickOf } from './config.js';\nimport { createWorld, command, step, finish, pack, unpack, health, cancel } from './sim.js';\nexport class Transport {\n constructor(hub,clock=()=>performance.now()){this.hub=hub;this.clock=clock;this.queue=[];this.tokens=26;this.refill=clock();this.lastSnap=-1000;this.stopped=false;this.metrics={sent:0,bytes:0,retries:0,rejected:0,maxBytes:0,maxSnapshot:0,packets:[]};}\n enqueue(data,options={}){if(this.stopped)return false;let raw;try{raw=JSON.stringify(data);}catch{this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n const bytes=new TextEncoder().encode(raw).length;if(bytes>16000){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n if(this.queue.length>=64){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}\n this.queue.push({data,options:{reliable:true,...options},bytes});return true;}\n send(data,options={}){const raw=JSON.stringify(data),bytes=new TextEncoder().encode(raw).length;if(bytes>16000){this.metrics.rejected++;return false;}return this.trySend({data,options,bytes});}\n trySend(m){if(this.stopped)return false;const now=this.clock();this.tokens=Math.min(26,this.tokens+(now-this.refill)*.014);this.refill=now;\n if(this.tokens<1)return false;\n if(\"'!this.hub.send(m.data,m.options)){this.metrics.retries++;return false;}\n this.tokens--;this.metrics.sent++;this.metrics.bytes+=m.bytes;this.metrics.maxBytes=Math.max(this.metrics.maxBytes,m.bytes);if(m.data.t==='\"'s')this.metrics.maxSnapshot=Math.max(this.metrics.maxSnapshot,m.bytes);\n this.metrics.packets.push([now,m.bytes,m.options.reliable\"'!==false]);if(this.metrics.packets.length>1000)this.metrics.packets.shift();return true;}\n flush(){while(this.queue.length&&this.trySend(this.queue[0]))this.queue.shift();}\n stop(){this.stopped=true;this.queue=[];}\n}\nexport class OnlineMatch {\n constructor(hub,{onWorld,onEnd,onEvent}={}){this.hub=hub;this.onWorld=onWorld;this.onEnd=onEnd;this.onEvent=onEvent;this.info=null;this.world=null;this.transport=new Transport(hub);this.started=false;this.ended=false;this.finished=false;this.seq=0;this.snapSeq=0;this.lastSeq=-1;this.ack=-1;this.lastSnapshot=-1000;this.lastBaseline=-10000;this.lastEvent=0;this.pendingFinish=false;this.intentStart=null;this.localPower=null;this.leavers=new Set();this.beginTimes=new Map();this.unsub=[];}\n async connect(){const info=await this.hub.connect({mode:'\"'shared-world',seats:[2,2]});if(\"'!info)return null;this.info=info;\n this.world=createWorld({mode:'\"'hub',court:4,seed:info.seed||71,duration:Math.min(180,(info.limitMs||180000)/1000)});this.seat=info.server?null:info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===info.me);if(this.seat<0)this.seat=null;\n const on=(event,fn)=>this.unsub.push(this.hub.on(event,fn));\n on('start',()=>{this.started=true;if(info.isHost)this.baseline();});\n on('message',(data,from)=>this.message(data,from));\n on('leave',({id})=>{this.leavers.add(id);const seat=info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===id);if(seat>=0&&info.isHost){cancel(this.world,seat,false);if(this.started&&\"'!this.finished)finish(this.world,'\"'opponent left',1-seat);this.pendingFinish=true;}});\n on('time-up',()=>{if(info.isHost&&\"'!this.finished){finish(this.world,'\"'timeout');this.pendingFinish=true;this.finalize();}});\n on('end',e=>{this.ended=true;this.transport.stop();this.intentStart=null;this.localPower=null;this.onEnd?.(e);});\n this.onWorld?.(this.world);this.hub.ready();return info;}\n intent(kind,stone){if(this.ended||\"'!this.started||this.hub.time()<0||this.seat===null)return false;\n const now=this.hub.time()/1000;const c={kind,seq:++this.seq,at:now};\n if(kind==='\"'stone')c.stone=stone;\n if(kind==='begin')this.intentStart=now;\n if(kind==='release'){c.duration=this.intentStart===null?0:clamp(now-this.intentStart,0,3);this.intentStart=null;}\n if(kind==='cancel')this.intentStart=null;\n if(this.info.isHost)return this.receiveIntent(c,this.info.me);\n return this.transport.enqueue({t:'c',c},{to:this.info.host});}\n receiveIntent(c,from){if(\"'!this.info.isHost||this.ended||!this.started||this.hub.time()<0||!c||typeof c!=='\"'object')return false;\n const seat=this.info.players.findIndex(p=>p.id===from);if(seat<0||this.leavers.has(from)||\"'!Number.isSafeInteger(c.seq)||!['\"'begin','release','cancel','stone'].includes(c.kind)||\"'!Number.isFinite(c.at))return false;\n const now=this.hub.time()/1000;if(c.at>now+.25||c.at<now-2.5)return false;\n if(c.kind==='\"'release'&&(\"'!Number.isFinite(c.duration)||c.duration<0||c.duration>3))return false;\n return command(this.world,seat,c);}\n message(m,from){if(this.ended||!m||typeof m!=='\"'object')return;\n if(this.info.isHost){if(m.t==='c')this.receiveIntent(m.c,from);else if(m.t==='ack'&&this.info.players.some(p=>p.id===from)&&Number.isInteger(m.n))this.ack=Math.max(this.ack,m.n);return;}\n if(from\"'!==this.info.host)return;\n if((m.t==='\"'b'||m.t==='s')&&m.v===1&&Number.isInteger(m.n)&&m.n>this.lastSeq){if(unpack(this.world,m)){this.lastSeq=m.n;if(m.t==='b')this.transport.enqueue({t:'ack',n:m.n},{to:this.info.host});}}\n if(m.t==='e'&&Number.isInteger(m.n)&&m.n>(this.eventSeq??-1)){this.eventSeq=m.n;for(const e of m.e||[])this.onEvent?.(e);}\n }\n baseline(){const p=pack(this.world,++this.snapSeq);p.t='b';this.transport.enqueue(p);this.lastBaseline=this.hub.time();}\n update(){if(this.ended||\"'!this.info)return;this.transport.flush();const ms=this.hub.time();if(!this.started||ms<0)return;\n if(this.info.isHost){\n  const target=Math.min(this.world.deadline,Math.floor(ms/1000/DT));let n=0;while(this.world.tick<target&&this.world.phase==='\"'playing'&&n++<600)step(this.world);\n  const events=this.world.events.splice(0);if(events.length){for(const e of events)this.onEvent?.(e);this.transport.enqueue({t:'e',n:++this.lastEvent,e:events.filter(e=>e.type\"'!=='\"'fall'||e.id%2===0)});}\n  if(ms-this.lastBaseline>=2000)this.baseline();\n  if(ms-this.lastSnapshot>=140&&this.transport.queue.length===0){const snap=pack(this.world,++this.snapSeq);if(JSON.stringify(snap).length<=1200){this.transport.send(snap,{reliable:false});}else this.transport.enqueue({...snap,t:'b'});this.lastSnapshot=ms;}\n  if(this.world.outcome&&\"'!this.finished){this.pendingFinish=true;this.finalize();}\n }\n this.transport.flush();}\n finalize(){if(!this.info?.isHost||this.finished||this.ended)return;const w=this.world;if(!w.outcome)finish(w,'\"'timeout');\n if(\"'!this.finalQueued){this.baseline();this.finalQueued=true;}this.transport.flush();if(this.transport.queue.length)return;\n const ids=this.info.players.map(p=>p.id).filter(id=>!this.leavers.has(id)),winner=w.outcome.winner,winid=winner>=0?this.info.players[winner]?.id:null;\n const standings=winner<0?[ids]:[ids.filter(id=>id===winid),ids.filter(id=>id!==winid)].filter(a=>a.length);\n const scores=Object.fromEntries(this.info.players.map((p,i)=>[p.id,Math.round(health(w,i)*1000)+w.players[i].score]));\n this.finished=true;this.hub.finish({standings,scores});this.pendingFinish=false;}\n dispose(){this.ended=true;this.transport.stop();for(const f of this.unsub)f();}\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/persistence.js <<'\"'EOF'\nexport const SAVE_KEY='smithereens-under-siege:tour:v1';\nexport function loadTour(storage){try{const s=JSON.parse(storage.getItem(SAVE_KEY));if(s?.version===1&&Number.isInteger(s.next)&&s.next>=1&&s.next<10&&Number.isInteger(s.seed)&&Array.isArray(s.totals)&&s.totals.length===2&&s.totals.every(n=>Number.isFinite(n)&&n>=0&&n<1e7)&&Array.isArray(s.results)&&s.results.length===s.next)return s;}catch{}return null;}\nexport function saveTour(storage,s){try{storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY,JSON.stringify({version:1,...s}));return true;}catch{return false;}}\nexport function eraseTour(storage){try{storage.removeItem(SAVE_KEY);}catch{}}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '297,365p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '535,572p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && rg -n 'addPlayer\\\\(|\\\\.padIndex|\\\\.pad =|padIndex' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -25 && rg -n 'SHELL_CSS|esh-ttl|esh-btns|esh-sh' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -14\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '297,365p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '535,572p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && rg -n 'addPlayer\\\\(|\\\\.padIndex|\\\\.pad =|padIndex' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -25 && rg -n 'SHELL_CSS|esh-ttl|esh-btns|esh-sh' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | head -14\"","aggregated_output":"- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'attack']). A step names actions joined by +: its directions are held exactly as it says (up, down, left, right; 'neutral' for none) as they change to that, its buttons pressed. A cheat code: input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'left', 'right', 'kick', 'attack'], { window: 3 })\n- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('confirm', near ? 'TALK' : null, near || talking)\n- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel). The keys held stay held (down() in the new layout, not pressed() again), and a press no step has seen counts in it\n- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on the touch stick) by its push, any other code held 1\n- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n- `input.clock = 0`: seconds of input time (the steps' dt added up)\n- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n- `input.invertMoveX`, `input.invertMoveY = false` †: the move stick turned round (the Controller settings)\n- `input.keysTo = null` †: the other players' inputs the keyboard's codes go to as well (players sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players)\n- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n- `input.screen`: the game's screen (mouse positions are read through it)\n- `input.steer = 'stick'` †: 'stick' (a stick drawn under the thumb) or 'drag' (a finger anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows the thumb)\n- `input.stick = [0, 0]` †: the touch stick's direction [x, y], length <= 1\n- `input.stickDeadzone = .12` †: the part of that radius a thumb moves before the stick counts (0..0.5)\n- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n- `input.stickOn = false` †: a finger is on it\n- `input.stickRadius = 44` †: how far (CSS pixels) a finger drags for full tilt\n- `input.stickSide = 'left'` †: 'left' or 'right', the half of the screen the stick lives on\n- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n- `input.zones = null` †: areas of the screen a finger holds an action down in, [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }] (fractions of the canvas, 0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's two halves, a rhythm game's lanes. A finger landing in one presses act until it lifts (several fingers, several zones), and starts no stick\n\n## 6. Pixel fonts\n\n- `E.font`: Pixel fonts. 'normal' (default) is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case; 'tiny' is the 3x5 upper-case font. text(g, str, x, y, color, opts) where opts is an outline color, false, or { font: 'normal' | 'tiny', outline: '#0b0814' | false, shadow: '#000' (1 px drop shadow), gradient: ['#fff', '#8ad'] (top to bottom), scale: 1, align: 'left' | 'center' | 'right', wrap: maxWidthPx, lineGap } '\\n' starts a new line. Returns { w, h } of the drawn block. title(...) draws big logo text.\n- `E.font.default` †: the font used when none is named: 'normal' (5 x 7) or 'tiny' (3 x 5)\n- `E.font.height(lines = 1, o, lineGap)`: the height in pixels of that many lines (with o's scale and font, and lineGap between them)\n- `E.font.lineHeight(o)`: pixels from one line to the next\n- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o: an outline color, or { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font }; returns { w, h }\n- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n- `game.gpu = null` †: the WebGPU lighting after enableGPU(), or null\n- `game.headless`: true for a game with no display (o.headless, or no DOM: Node)\n- `game.hitstop = 0`: seconds of hit-stop left (freeze: a scene's entry ends it)\n- `game.hz = 60`: the display's refresh rate, measured\n- `game.input`: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...)\n- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in draw)\n- `game.live` †: true (o.live): a pause opens the menus over a world that keeps stepping (an online or shared world can't stop for one player): paused is true and the scene's update goes on, the menu holding the player's own input back\n- `game.o`: the options the game was made with, the defaults filled in (view, res, expand, minW, minH, maxW, maxH, bg, step, input, loop, headless)\n- `game.particles`: dust, sparks, debris and text in the world\n- `game.pauseOverlay = true`: false hides the engine's PAUSED overlay (a game drawing its own pause screen)\n- `game.pauseReason = null`: why the game paused: 'player' | 'focus' (the page was hidden) | 'controller' (unplugged) | 'menu', or null\n- `game.paused = false`: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update)\n- `game.r`: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless)\n- `game.real = 0`: seconds the game has stepped through, pauses and hit-stop included (blinking HUD, notes)\n- `game.reduceMotion`: the player asked for less motion (prefers-reduced-motion): shake and flashes are softened\n- `game.scene = null`: the scene running\n- `game.sceneName = null`: its name ('main' for a game started with one scene)\n- `game.scenes = null`: the scenes given to start(), by name\n- `game.screen`: the low-resolution screen (its W, H, scale and buffer)\n- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n- `game.stats`: per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays\n- `game.stats.updateMs`, `game.stats.renderMs`: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing\n- `game.stats.frameMs`: the real time since the last frame\n- `game.stats.steps`: the updates it ran\n- `game.stats.items`: what it queued for drawing\n- `game.stats.actors`: actors drawn\n- `game.stats.culled`: actors skipped off screen\n- `game.time = 0`: game seconds since start (it stops during pause and hit-stop, and slows with timeScale)\n- `game.timeScale = 1`: game speed, 1 normal, .25 slow motion, 0 stopped (it outlives a scene change: a game's speed setting; restore a slow motion with a kept timer)\n- `game.view`: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView)\n- `game.views`: views this game is designed for (view cycling and the checker use it). null = every view\n- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen instead, as a report a player can screenshot\n\n## 10b. Standard features\n777:    /** deadzone: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8); padIndex, padId: the gamepad in use (null\n780:    this.deadzone = .18; this.padIndex = null; this.padId = ''; this.lastDevice = 'keyboard';\n784:    this.pad = 'any'; this.keysTo = null; this._claimed = null;\n943:    const k = clamp(strength, 0, 1) * clamp(this.rumbleScale, 0, 1); if (!(k > 0) || this.padIndex === null || !this.screen.canvas) return false;\n944:    let a = null; try { const p = navigator.getGamepads()[this.padIndex]; a = p && p.vibrationActuator; } catch (e) { /* gamepads blocked */ }\n1171:    const C = this._claimed, ok = p => p && p.connected !== false && (this.pad === 'any' ? !(C && C.has(p.index)) : p.index === this.pad);   // (its own pad, or any another player hasn't)\n1172:    const p = this.pad === null ? null : Array.from(pads || []).find(p => ok(p) && p.index === this.padIndex) || Array.from(pads || []).find(ok);\n1174:    if (!p || p.index !== this.padIndex || p.id !== this.padId) {\n1175:      if (!p && this.padIndex !== null) { this.padLost = this.lastDevice 