{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> artifacts/decision-log.md <<'EOF'\n# Decision log\n- Native 2D full engine 0.89.1; no vendor engine patches. Artillery kit supplied the fixed-step, trajectory evaluation and native shell/terrain patterns. Walking, free aim, turns, rockets, inventory and auto-fire were replaced.\n- World coordinates: x across the lane, z up; engine y is decorative depth. Terrain's height coordinate is mapped only in its native draw boundary. Cosmetic chunks never own castle collision.\n- A 960-unit arena, 50° elevation, 530 u/s full launch speed and 260 u/s² gravity make full charge overshoot; useful charge is roughly two-thirds. All tensions share the range. Per-projectile gravity is captured at launch.\n- Predict/live use the same swept ballistic integrator. AI searches that integrator and submits legal begin/release/stone commands. Seeded combat randomness never depends on decorative rig/blink randomness.\n- Hub packets contain full compact health strings, so losing any unreliable snapshot is repaired by the next. Reliable baselines start/resync and require passive ACKs. 140 ms snapshots; a local 14 msg/s token budget leaves headroom below the Hub's aggregate 20/s budget.\n- Hold-duration reconciliation is bounded to authoritative elapsed begin time ±0.32 seconds, then the legal 0–1 power curve. Commands are monotonic and authenticated by sender ID. Local charge feedback starts immediately; clients never report damage or score.\n- Developer gravity affects new projectiles/predictions, timing affects the next action, health scaling preserves existing fractions. All local mutations mark the run; Hub diagnostics expose no mutation route.\n- The original source label is retained verbatim. European archive dates it 1981; US manual copyright is 1982. No invented reconciliation.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Smithereens Under Siege\n\nOpen the root single-file HTML directly in a browser. It is self-contained and works offline. To host online versus, import it into AI Hub; the standalone game has no matchmaking service.\n\n- Hold/release Cross, Space or the left mouse button to sling. L1/R1 or Q/E select stone. Circle/C/right mouse cancels. Options/Escape pauses.\n- Two keyboard seats: Teal uses Space and Q/E; Coral uses Right Shift and U/O (I cancels). Local setup also offers two pads or keyboard plus pad.\n- Touch: hold/release on the field. Portrait keeps the full lane and magnifies the opposing castle.\n- Pause → Developer tools opens scenarios, stepping, live tuning and the versioned court editor. These changes mark local runs. Hub exposes read-only diagnostics.\n\nFrom this development folder:\n\n\"'```\nnpm run build\nnpm run verify\n```\n\nVerification prints failures and a single count. It covers deterministic combat and a complete ten-bout tour, real file loading/input/audio, and the unmodified official Hub harness (normal, impairment, host leave, server host). Browser tests use the already-installed Python Playwright environment. No npm runtime dependencies are required.\n\nPinned engine: my-3D2dge 0.89.1, 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Hub: protocol 1/client 1.4.0, 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Both upstream revisions matched at acquisition. Original source research and attribution appear in About/Credits. All audio is generated in code; physical hardware and acoustic quality are unconfirmed.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> artifacts/decision-log.md <<'EOF'\n# Decision log\n- Native 2D full engine 0.89.1; no vendor engine patches. Artillery kit supplied the fixed-step, trajectory evaluation and native shell/terrain patterns. Walking, free aim, turns, rockets, inventory and auto-fire were replaced.\n- World coordinates: x across the lane, z up; engine y is decorative depth. Terrain's height coordinate is mapped only in its native draw boundary. Cosmetic chunks never own castle collision.\n- A 960-unit arena, 50° elevation, 530 u/s full launch speed and 260 u/s² gravity make full charge overshoot; useful charge is roughly two-thirds. All tensions share the range. Per-projectile gravity is captured at launch.\n- Predict/live use the same swept ballistic integrator. AI searches that integrator and submits legal begin/release/stone commands. Seeded combat randomness never depends on decorative rig/blink randomness.\n- Hub packets contain full compact health strings, so losing any unreliable snapshot is repaired by the next. Reliable baselines start/resync and require passive ACKs. 140 ms snapshots; a local 14 msg/s token budget leaves headroom below the Hub's aggregate 20/s budget.\n- Hold-duration reconciliation is bounded to authoritative elapsed begin time ±0.32 seconds, then the legal 0–1 power curve. Commands are monotonic and authenticated by sender ID. Local charge feedback starts immediately; clients never report damage or score.\n- Developer gravity affects new projectiles/predictions, timing affects the next action, health scaling preserves existing fractions. All local mutations mark the run; Hub diagnostics expose no mutation route.\n- The original source label is retained verbatim. European archive dates it 1981; US manual copyright is 1982. No invented reconciliation.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Smithereens Under Siege\n\nOpen the root single-file HTML directly in a browser. It is self-contained and works offline. To host online versus, import it into AI Hub; the standalone game has no matchmaking service.\n\n- Hold/release Cross, Space or the left mouse button to sling. L1/R1 or Q/E select stone. Circle/C/right mouse cancels. Options/Escape pauses.\n- Two keyboard seats: Teal uses Space and Q/E; Coral uses Right Shift and U/O (I cancels). Local setup also offers two pads or keyboard plus pad.\n- Touch: hold/release on the field. Portrait keeps the full lane and magnifies the opposing castle.\n- Pause → Developer tools opens scenarios, stepping, live tuning and the versioned court editor. These changes mark local runs. Hub exposes read-only diagnostics.\n\nFrom this development folder:\n\n\"'```\nnpm run build\nnpm run verify\n```\n\nVerification prints failures and a single count. It covers deterministic combat and a complete ten-bout tour, real file loading/input/audio, and the unmodified official Hub harness (normal, impairment, host leave, server host). Browser tests use the already-installed Python Playwright environment. No npm runtime dependencies are required.\n\nPinned engine: my-3D2dge 0.89.1, 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Hub: protocol 1/client 1.4.0, 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Both upstream revisions matched at acquisition. Original source research and attribution appear in About/Credits. All audio is generated in code; physical hardware and acoustic quality are unconfirmed.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
