{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_97","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/browser_verify.py';s=open(p).read();old=\\\"page.goto((root/'artifacts/game.html').as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__SIEGE?.world');page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\\";new=\\\"page.goto((root.parent/(json.loads((root/'build-info.json').read_text())['base']+'.html')).as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__SIEGE?.world');page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\\";assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new,1);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat ../PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_97","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/browser_verify.py';s=open(p).read();old=\\\"page.goto((root/'artifacts/game.html').as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__SIEGE?.world');page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\\";new=\\\"page.goto((root.parent/(json.loads((root/'build-info.json').read_text())['base']+'.html')).as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__SIEGE?.world');page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\\";assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new,1);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat ../PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Smithereens Under Siege — build progress\n\n## Contract and paths\n- Build `PLAN.md`; deliver names/report schema from `TASK.md`.\n- Source label: Stone Sling Smithereens - 1980 (manual says 1982; European archive says 1981; retain supplied label).\n- Title selected privately from 50 riffs with `node:crypto.randomInt`: **Smithereens Under Siege**.\n- Development folder / output basename: `Smithereens-Under-Siege-Stone-Sling-Smithereens-1980-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-032856`.\n- Final root artifacts: basename `.html`, `exit-interview.json`; this log remains in root.\n- Engine current revision verified: `8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691` (0.89.1).\n- Hub current revision verified: `35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869` (client 1.4.0).\n- Read game-toolchain skill. Native 2D/code-defined assets and code audio; no raster-generation dependency.\n- Do not inspect adjacent runs, touch parent repository changes, use shared temporary space, or stop others' processes.\n\n## Completed\n- Read all TASK.md and PLAN.md requirements.\n- Source research: official Smithereens manual, source archive/review. Preserve charging, interruptions, ten-bout weighted scoring; new mechanics identified as original.\n- Verified current upstream SHAs with gh.\n\n## In progress / next\n- Implemented source modules under the development folder: config/content, shared simulation, native view, native-bus audio, app/UI, persistence, Hub adapter, metadata.\n- Build works: `npm run build` emits root artifact plus identical `artifacts/game.html` test copy. No runtime external requests.\n- Native Node suite passed **62 checks, 0 failures**, including every court/stone target reachability, every isolated last fragment, same-tick draw, recovery/dedup, snapshots, full ten-bout tour via app entry/results/replay, exact attract threshold/loop and saved-state isolation.\n- Initial Chromium file:// input/play run had zero runtime/game errors. Captures in `artifacts/title.png` and `charge.png`; initial visual defects fixed, needs recapture.\n- Browser suite passed **133 checks, 0 failures** including real game-specific charge/release with rejected-send retries, under 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss, both ordinary and no-local-player server hosts. All six official harness rounds passed.\n- Added a deterministic network simulator (2 checks passed) for asymmetric command delay, lost/reordered snapshots, stale-baseline ACKs, exactly-once finish, sender ownership, packet sizes and post-end silence.\n- Added final-artifact/metadata checks (3 passed): parse scripts, unchanged first Hub client, ten source modules inlined, no external runtime paths, exact report schema and catalogue consistency.\n- Closed surface gaps during review: isolated voice slider, functional TV scale, full imported block preservation, stronger tour-save validation, persistent developer-run marking, attract-only authored weapon goals. Attract now demonstrates all three stones plus crew/launcher interruption, recovery, collapse and three courts in its 90-second loop.\n- Source formatting uses Biome; build parser now handles formatted multiline imports and parses the bundle before publishing. No engine/vendor source changes.\n- `exit-interview.json` now generated from final `src/metadata.js`; needs final combined suite after latest refinements.\n- Visual recapture running as shell session **71329** was completed; new recapture in current turn. Native stopped games require `{ draw: true }` for captures, corrected visual script. Phone inset now copies the current native frame during rendering.\n- Requirement/acceptance ledger written to `artifacts/requirements.md`; decisions in `artifacts/decision-log.md`.\n- Final code review added explicit queue slots for cancel/final packets, a tested player-leave result, correct mouse world-coordinate conversion at native zoom, visible repair hammers and eased crew withdrawal/return.\n- Latest affected checks: 7 network/artifact/native-repair checks passed; **141 browser checks, 0 failures** after all latest functional changes.\n- Full suite now running as session **67291**. Command: `npm run verify > artifacts/verify-final.log 2>&1`. It rebuilds HTML/interview itself. The previous full suite passed 207 checks; current expected count is 209 after two added checks. The complete-tour driver now fixes seed 71 through observation/setup while retaining real entry/commands/outcomes.\n- After it completes: read the final log, verify root artifact/interview, update this log to completed with actual counts, then hand over game plus concise required four reporting groups. Do not keep adding features or rerunning unchanged checks.\n\n## Verification / issue ledger\n1. Authored lakeside row exceeded castle bounds (low severity); court validator caught it; fixed row to eight columns; all five court validators now pass.\n2. Initial title displayed empty combat HUD/inset (presentation); screenshot found it; HUD starts hidden now.\n3. TV title menu extended below frame (usability); screenshot found it; reduced native-scaled title typography/spacing. Browser bounds check pending.\n4. Charge cleanup consumed Escape before the engine handled pause (critical/game-breaking); browser regression caught it. Cancel input and open native pause in the proper hook order. Regression and local/Hub pause checks passed.\n5. Portrait menu corner covered the opponent score (presentation/usability); phone visual review caught it. Moved portrait score plates below the corner; phone/tablet overlap regression passed.\n- Additional code-review fixes: stale-baseline ACK even after a newer snapshot, editor import preserving geometry, code bundler accepting formatted multiline imports. These are not counted as testing-found game bugs.\n- Current testing-found game bug count: **5**, including **1 critical**, all fixed. Metadata/interview/About now agree.\n- Test infrastructure corrections (not game defects): Python visual script named `inspect.py` shadowed stdlib, renamed; Node `process.chdir` needs string, corrected. Do not count these as game bugs.\n\n## Decisions\n- Use full native engine and replace artillery kit rules with shared fixed-step combat. No external runtime dependencies planned.\n- No delegated agents: build is kept under one integrator.\n\n## Reporting\n- Exact date 2026-11-06 03:28:56; model OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max; environment Codex CLI (headless); Linux; usage `added on import`.\n- All Source Information + 4 Testing Feedback + 6 Engine Feedback + 4 Prompt Feedback answers must appear in game, interview, final reply.\n- Be candid about hardware stand-ins and unlistened acoustic quality.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
